85]\n* [ Platter Trays ][86]\n* [Overhead shot of lots of chilled food packaging solutions on black table. Includes boxes and\npots, all filled with different salads.][Overhead shot of lots of chilled food packaging\nsolutions on black table. Includes boxes and pots, all filled with different salads.]\n\nChilled Food-to-Go\n\n[Chilled Food-to-Go][87] Back\n* [ Salad Pots ][88]\n* [ Salad Boxes ][89]\n* [Range of kraft hot food-to-go packaging in black hot cabinet, including Stagione, Savori pillow\npacks, and souper pots, with contents details in front of each packaging type.][Range of kraft\nhot food-to-go packaging in black hot cabinet, including Stagione, Savori pillow packs, and\nsouper pots, with contents details in front of each packaging type.]\n\nHot Food-to-Go\n\n[Hot Food-to-Go][90] Back\n* [ Pots ][91]\n* [ Boxes ][92]\n* [ Trays ][93]\n* [ Cones & Scoops ][94]\n* [ Hot Sandwich Packs ][95]\n* [Takeaway food packaging on wooden table, being eaten from. Filled with prawns, sushi, salad,\ncurry, noodles, and tomato pasta with meatballs.][Takeaway food packaging on wooden table, being\neaten from. Filled with prawns, sushi, salad, curry, noodles, and tomato pasta with meatballs.]\n\nDelivered Food\n\n[Delivered Food][96] Back\n* [ Boxes ][97]\n* [ Pots ][98]\n* [Selection of Colpac&apos;s sustainable party food packaging including meal boxes and paperboard\ntoys, surrounded by balloons and streamers.][Selection of Colpac's sustainable party food\npackaging including meal boxes and paperboard toys, surrounded by balloons and streamers.]\n\nParty Packaging\n\n[Party Packaging][99] Back\n* [ Meal Box Kits ][100]\n* [ Patterned Meal Boxes ][101]\n* [ Seasonal Meal Boxes ][102]\n* [ Coloured Meal Boxes ][103]\n* [ Combi Trays ][104]\n* [ [Spread of bakery packaging including small kraft slice boxes, white boxes full of cupcakes,\ndressed with cake stand, wooden board, and pink and white celebration cake.][Spread of bakery\npackaging including small kraft slice boxes, white boxes full of cupcakes, dressed with cake\nstand, wooden board, and pink and white celebration cake.]\n\nBakery Packaging\n\n][105]\n* [ [Heat seal packaging for sandwiches in silver machine, about to be heat sealed by machine\noperative.][Heat seal packaging for sandwiches in silver machine, about to be heat sealed by\nmachine operative.]\n\nPackaging Machinery\n\n][106]\n* [Overhead shot of black Combione salad tray, Colpac special offers product, in chilled cabinet.\nFilled with sweetcorn, plum tomatoes, and salad leaves.][Overhead shot of black Combione salad\ntray, Colpac special offers product, in chilled cabinet. Filled with sweetcorn, plum tomatoes,\nand salad leaves.]\n\nClearance\n\n[Clearance][107] Back\n* [ Sandwich Packs ][108]\n* [ Chilled Food-to-Go ][109]\n* [ Hot Food-to-Go ][110]\n* [ Party ][111]\n* [ Drinks ][112]\n* [ About ][113]\n* [ About ][114]\n[About][115] Back\n* [ About Us ][116]\n* [ Food Packaging Certifications ][117]\n* [ Markets ][118]\n[Markets][119] Back\n* [ Food Delivery Packaging ][120]\n* [ QSR Packaging ][121]\n* [ Retail Food Packaging ][122]\n* [ Travel Packaging ][123]\n* [ Bespoke ][124]\n[Bespoke][125] Back\n* [ Custom Food Packaging ][126]\n* [ Case Studies ][127]\n* [ Brands ][128]\n[Brands][129] Back\n* [ Clasp\u00ae ][130]\n* [ Multi-Food Pots ][131]\n* [ Stagione\u00ae ][132]\n* [ Souper Pots ][133]\n* [ Zest\u2122 ][134]\n* [ Sustainability ][135]\n* [ Extended Producer Responsibility (EPR) ][136]\n* [ Business as a Force for Good ][137]\n* [ Packaging Sustainability ][138]\n* [ Recyclable Food Packaging ][139]\n* [ Compostable Food Packaging ][140]\n* [ Resources ][141]\n* [ News ][142]\n[News][143] Back\n* [ Certifications ][144]\n* [ Company ][145]\n* [ Products ][146]\n* [ Sustainability ][147]\n* [ See all News ][148]\n* [ FAQs ][149]\n[FAQs][150] Back\n* [ Operations ][151]\n* [ Product ][152]\n* [ Sales ][153]\n* [ Sustainability ][154]\n* [ See all FAQs ][155]\n* [ Case Studies ][156]\n[Case Studies][157] Back\n* [ Chilled Food-to-Go ][158]\n* [ Delivered Food ][159]\n* [ Hot Food-to-Go ][160]\n* [ Sandwich Packaging ][161]\n* [ See all Case Studies ][162]\n* [ Resources ][163]\n[Resources][164] Back\n* [ Catalogues ][165]\n* [ Flyers ][166]\n* [ Videos ][167]\n* [ See all Resources ][168]\n* [ Contact ][169]\n[Packaging Selector][170] [View Sabert catalogue][171]\n[Packaging Selector][172]\n\n### Pret A Manger\n\n# Colpac pioneered the use of groundbreaking direct food contact ink technology, to eliminate added\n# plastic.\n\n[Overhead shot of four kraft Pret platter bases in different sizes. Filled with mince pies, small\nbaguettes, sandwich triangles, and brownie bites. Platter bases on wooden surface.][Overhead shot of\nfour kraft Pret platter bases in different sizes. Filled with mince pies, small baguettes, sandwich\ntriangles, and brownie bites. Platter bases on wooden surface.]\n\nPret were looking to reduce plastic from the platters used to package their fresh, hand delivered\nfood. Partnering with Colpac, the teams developed platter bases using direct food contact inks, the\nfirst project of its kind in foodservice.\n\nThe [previous iteration of Pret\u2019s platter bases][173] were made from paperboard and included a\nlaminate coating to the interior to protect food contents. To support sustainability goals and\nimprove pack recyclability, Colpac developed a solution that worked with direct food contact inks,\ninstead of the plastic barrier.\n\nExtensive tests were conducted to ensure the ink application and coatings met required safety\nstandards and KIT (grease resistance) and COBB (water absorption) ratings. Pret also conducted\nin-house trials to meet demanding kitchen requirements, even using astringent ingredients such as\nlemon juice, avocado and mayonnaise. This due diligence, alongside utilising realistic printed kraft\neffect paperboard, achieved Pret\u2019s high presentation standards and maintained pack functionality to\nsuit Pret\u2019s fast-paced kitchen environments and consumer preferences.\n\nSimpler recycling was achieved through replacing fibreboard composite materials (amber in Recycling\nAssessment Methodology (RAM)) with uncoated paperboard (green in RAM) and direct food contact inks,\nresulting in 0% plastic content and recyclability through any paper re-pulping process. To enhance\nthe platters even further, and to improve resource efficiency, the paperboard was optimised to a\nlighter, [FSC^{\u00ae} certified][174] board, proving sustainable sourcing and further reducing material\nusage.\n\nReplacing plastic laminate with direct food contact inks is projected to save 1936kg* of plastic and\n7471kg* of paperboard, equating to 9407kg* of packaging material savings/year.\n\nThe platter bases fit within the \u2018paper or board\u2019 category for the latest [Extended Producer\nResponsibility][175] (EPR) regulation, reducing material category fees by \u00a3240 per tonne. As a\nresult of this, together with the additional lightweighting to use less paperboard, the projected\nEPR unit cost for Pret\u2019s platter bases has been reduced by an impressive 55%.\n\n> \u201cWe have built a solid partnership with Colpac and we continue to be impressed with the team\u2019s\n> dedication to creating the best possible solutions to present our fresh food. The new platters\n> look superb, and the premise of this project truly represents our pledges to make our packaging\n> 100% recyclable and to eliminate all unnecessary single-use plastic.\u201d\n> Simon Oxley, Global Head of Packaging at Pret\n\nConsistent communication and thorough attention to detail from Colpac\u2019s account management, quality,\nand production teams, resulted in this new packaging concept to be brought to the market in 2024.\nFollowing successful in-store trials, the packs are planned to be rolled out across additional Pret\noutlets worldwide.\n\n*Weights are calculated based on Pret\u2019s annual usage.\n\n##### [Contact us][176]\n\n## Case Studies\n\nLooking for inspiration? Take a look at some of our previous work.\n\n[Two wedge sandwich packs in yellow and blue, and one square sandwich pack in green, on turfed pitch\nsurface with net in background.][Two wedge sandwich packs in yellow and blue, and one square\nsandwich pack in green, on turfed pitch surface with net in background.]\nSandwich Packaging\n\n### Levy UK\n\nAn All-Paper Packaging Solution for World-Class Events.\n\n][177]\n[Stagione pot, filled with "
