            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[[Owens & Minor][Owens & Minor]][2]\n* [Distribution & Logistics][3]\n* Close\n* [Distribution & Logistics][4]\n* * [3PL Services][5]\n* [Customer-Owned Inventory Management][6]\n* [Emergency & Pandemic Preparedness][7]\n* [Expanded Access Standardization][8]\n* * [Logical Unit of Measure (LUM)][9]\n* [OMFreight+][10]\n* [Supplier Management][11]\n* [Supply Chain Consulting][12]\n* [Procedural Services][13]\n* Close\n* [Procedural Services][14]\n* * [QSight][15]\n* [QSight Tissue Management][16]\n* [QSight Kanban][17]\n* [QSight RFID][18]\n* [QSight Bill Only Management][19]\n* * [Medical Kitting Services][20]\n* [SurgiTrack: Unitized Delivery][21]\n* [PANDAC: Suture Management][22]\n* [Proprietary Products][23]\n* [About][24]\n* Close\n* * [Leadership][25]\n* [Sustainability][26]\n* * [Careers][27]\n* [Ethics And Compliance][28]\n* [Newsroom][29]\n* [Insights][30]\n* [Insights][31]\n* Close\n* [Insights][32]\n* * TOPICS\n* [Services][33]\n* Close\n* Principles of Antibiotic Stewardship: Impacting Every Patient\n[Learn More][34]\nImproving the Cath Lab Through RFID Technology\n[Learn More][35]\nPrinciples of Evidence-Based Purchasing of Infection Control Products and Services\n[Learn More][36]\nThe Evolving Role of Infection Prevention and Control in Healthcare\n[Learn More][37]\n[More Topics][38]\n* [Inventory Management][39]\n* Close\n* [Kanban: a simple, effective solution to consumable supply management in the\nhospital][Kanban: a simple, effective solution to consumable supply management in the\nhospital]\nKanban: a simple, effective solution to consumable supply management in the hospital\n[Learn More][40]\n[Kanban Inventory Management][Kanban Inventory Management]\nKanban: How to extend its value through technology solution integration\n[Learn More][41]\n[Kanban Inventory Management][Kanban Inventory Management]\nDispelling 5 Myths About Kanban in Hospital Inventory Management\n[Learn More][42]\n[Owens & Minor Supply Chain][Owens & Minor Supply Chain]\nWhy Seamless IT Solution Integration is Essential for Hospitals\n[Learn More][43]\n[More Topics][44]\n* [Healthcare Logistics][45]\n* Close\n* Four Ways Healthcare Logistics Helps Build Resilient Supply Chains\n[Learn More][46]\n[More Topics][47]\n* [Consulting][48]\n* Close\n* [More Topics][49]\n* [Infection Prevention][50]\n* Close\n* Principles of Antibiotic Stewardship: Impacting Every Patient\n[Learn More][51]\nPrinciples of Evidence-Based Purchasing of Infection Control Products and Services\n[Learn More][52]\nThe Evolving Role of Infection Prevention and Control in Healthcare\n[Learn More][53]\nStopping Life-Threatening Sepsis in its Tracks: An Imminent Threat to Patient Safety\n[Learn More][54]\n[More Topics][55]\n* [Contact Us][56]\n* [Search][57]\n* Close\n* Search\n\n# Sustainability\n\n[Home][58]\n[About Us][59]\nSustainability\n\n## Our Sustainability Priorities\n\nSince our founding in 1882, Owens & Minor has remained committed to our teammates, customers, and\ncommunities where we conduct business. We recognize the need to identify, prioritize, and\nmanage non-financial impacts from our operations.\n\n*In 2021, we completed our first sustainability materiality assessment to identify and prioritize\ntopics most relevant to our key stakeholders. Using the results of this assessment, we developed a\nframework to align ESG risks and opportunities with our overall business strategy.\nOur Sustainability Framework forms the basis of our program, integrating the\npriorities identified in our materiality assessment into key aspects of our operations. This\nframework is grounded in our Mission and emphasizes the importance of\nincorporating sustainability commitments into our culture and values.*\n\n## Sustainability Governance\n\nTo effectively manage the implementation of our sustainability strategy, Owens & Minor developed a\nsustainability governance structure designed to define our framework and deliver on our commitments.\nA Sustainability Governing Board, composed of members of the Executive Leadership Team, oversees the\nESG programming. A Sustainability Steering Committee, composed of top-line leadership from business\nsegments across the organization, implements sustainability priorities and recommends policies and\npractices that conform to our sustainability strategy. There are also several working-level\ncommittees that manage ESG activities within the company.\n\n## Promoting Environmental Stewardship\n\nWe work to minimize the impact of our operations on the environment. To minimize climate risk, we\nproactively review our facilities and supply chain and monitor climate-related threats and\nopportunities to ensure continuity of our supply and operations. We manage our carbon footprint\nthrough fleet efficiency goals and a dedicated emissions reduction working group. We seek to reduce\nwaste from our operations by improving our packaging and labelling, in-house scrap reuse in\nmanufacturing processes, and by building recycling partnerships with our customers. We strive to\nresponsibly manage water as a shared resource with award-winning wastewater treatment processes and\nefficiency enhancements in our use of process water.\n\nAs part of our commitment to minimizing our environmental footprint, in 2022, Owens & Minor\ncommitted to two climate goals:\n1. 50% reduction in Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions by 2030\n2. Net zero Scope 1 and Scope 2 emissions by 2050\n\n## Climate Resilience Plan\n\nAs part of our efforts to buffer against climate risk, we are proud to share a Climate Resilience\nPlan for Continuous Operations outlining our strategies to manage the climate impacts of our\nbusiness and to identify and address prospective risks to our business brought on by climate change.\n\n[ Climate Resilience Plan ][60]\n\n## Caring for Our Customers and Communities\n\nWe deliver superior service and innovative solutions for our customers and the communities we\nsupport. To maintain product quality and meet regulatory requirements, we have a dedicated team of\nQuality Assurance and Regulatory Affairs professionals to oversee the product lifecycle. We invest\nin the communities where we operate by encouraging our teammates\u2019 volunteerism. Through our\ninnovative healthcare solutions, we build stronger communities, develop integrated solutions with\nour partners, collaborate to enable supply chain continuity, and support healthcare to focus on\ncomplex patient needs.\n\n## Operating Responsibly\n\nWe strive to demonstrate sound governance, accountability, and responsible sourcing. Owens & Minor\nmaintains a Code of Honor as part of our comprehensive Compliance and Ethics Program and monitors\ncorruption and bribery risk through our Internal Audit, Procurement, Compliance, and Vendor\nRelations Teams. To safeguard against cybersecurity risk and ensure data privacy, we model our\ncybersecurity program to align with practices and standards referenced within the NIST Cybersecurity\nFramework.\n\n[ Our Ethics & Compliance Program ][61]\n\n## Empowering Our Teammates\n\nOwens & Minor fosters an empowering, safe, diverse, and inclusive work environment where all\nteammates can thrive. We strive to empower our teammates by ensuring there are open channels of\ncommunication across all levels of the organization. We provide learning resources and tools\ndesigned to support teammates in developing skills for their role and planning their career paths.\nThrough our annual talent review, we offer leadership development opportunities to increase the\nreadiness of top talent leaders to assume greater responsibility at Owens & Minor.\n\nOn December 31, 2025, Owens & Minor, Inc. concluded the sales of its Products & Healthcare Services\nbusiness to Platinum Equity. Prior to this separation, corporate sustainability reporting included\nboth companies. While historic Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) reports are provided\nbelow, this information should not be compared to future information given the material change in\ncompany structure. Going forward, all sustainability reporting will include information only for\nOwens & Minor.\n\n### 2025 Impact Report\n\n[Owens & Minor 2025 ESG Report][Owens & Minor 2025 ESG Report]\n\n[2025 Impact Report][62]\n\n### 2024 Impact Report\n\n[owens-minor-2024-impact-report][owens-minor-2024-impact-report]\n\n[2024 Impact Report][63]\n\n### 2023 ESG Report\n\n[Owens & Minor Love Takes Care][Owens & Minor Love Takes Care]\n\n[2023 ESG Report][64]\n[2023 ESG Report Content Matrices Index][65]\n\n### 2022 ESG Report\n\n[Owens & Minor Love Takes Care][Owens & Minor Love Takes Care]\n\n[2022 ESG Report][66]\n[2022 ESG Report Content Matrix][67]\n* * Customer Portals\n* * [Bill Only Management][68]\n* [OM MarketPlace][69]\n* * [QSight][70]\n* * Connect With Us\n* * [Contact Us][71]\n* [Careers][72]\n* * Follow Us\n* [Facebook][73]\n* [\ud835\udd4fX][74]\n* [Linkedin][75]\n* [Instagram][76]\n\n\u00a9 2026. All rights reserved.\n* [Website Terms of Use][77]\n* [Privacy Policy][78]\n* [Web Content Statement][79]\n* [Transparency in Coverage \u2013 UHC][80]\n* [Glossary][81]\n* [Sitemap][82]\n* [CA SB 261][83]\n* [Owens & Minor FAQ][84]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: https://www.owens-minor.com/\n[3]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/\n[4]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/\n[5]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/3pl-services/\n[6]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/customer-owned-inventory-management/\n[7]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/emergency-pandemic-preparedness/\n[8]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/expanded-access-standardization/\n[9]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/lum/\n[10]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/omfreightplus/\n[11]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/supplier-management/\n[12]: https://www.owens-minor.com/distribution/consulting/\n[13]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/\n[14]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/\n[15]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/qsight/\n[16]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/qsight/tissue-management/\n[17]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/qsight/qsight-kanban/\n[18]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/qsight/qsight-rfid/\n[19]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/bill-only/\n[20]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/medical-kitting-services/\n[21]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/surgitrack-unitized-delivery/\n[22]: https://www.owens-minor.com/services/pandac/\n[23]: https://www.owens-minor.com/products/\n[24]: https://www.owens-minor.com/about/\n[25]: https://www.owens-minor.com/?page_id=1022645\n[26]: https://www.owens-minor.com/about/sustainability/\n[27]: https://www.owens-minor.com/about/careers/\n[28]: https://compliance.owens-minor.com/\n[29]: https://www.owens-minor.com/press/\n[30]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/\n[31]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/\n[32]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/\n[33]: https://www.owens-minor.com/topic/services/\n[34]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/principles-of-antibiotic-stewardship-impacting-every-pati\nent/\n[35]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/improving-the-cath-lab-through-rfid-technology/\n[36]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/principles-of-evidence-based-purchasing-of-infection-cont\nrol-products-and-services/\n[37]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/the-evolving-role-of-infection-prevention-and-control-in-\nhealthcare/\n[38]: /about/news-pr/\n[39]: https://www.owens-minor.com/topic/inventory-management/\n[40]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/kanban-a-simple-effective-solution-to-consumable-supply-m\nanagement-in-the-hospital/\n[41]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/kanban-how-to-extend-value-through-technology-solution-in\ntegration/\n[42]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/5-myths-about-kanban-in-hospital-inventory-management/\n[43]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/seamless-it-solution-integration-is-a-must-have-for-hospi\ntals/\n[44]: /about/news-pr/\n[45]: https://www.owens-minor.com/topic/healthcare-logistics/\n[46]: https://www.owens-minor.com/insights/four-ways-healthcare-logistics-helps-build-resilient-supp\nly-chains/\n[47]: /about/news-pr/\n[48]: https://www.owens-minor.com/topic/resource-management/\n[49]: /about/new"
