        "crawl_text": "[Skip to content][1]\n[[PCM packs]][2] PHASE CHANGE MATERIAL\nToggle navigation\n* [Home][3]\n* [Industry Challenges][4]\n  * [Common Sample Type & Recommended Shipping][5]\n* [Resources][6]\n  * [Faq][7]\n  * [Blog][8]\n* [Products][9]\n  * [Cool Packs][10]\n  * [Ice Packs][11]\n  * [Freezer Packs][12]\n  * [CRT Packs][13]\n  * [Ambient Packs][14]\n* [Contact][15]\n\n\u00a0\n\nManufacturer for **savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs**, a sustainable series of phase change material based cold\nchain refrigerants.\n\nProtect your diagnostic and clinical trial samples from the risks of temperature excursion by\ntransporting them with **savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs**, a sustainable series of phase change material-based\ncold chain refrigerants.\n\n[home banner]\n\n# Reduce the risk of temperature excursions with savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs\n\n## **What happens when samples are exposed to extreme temperatures?**\n1. **Delay of frozen samples shipped on dry-ice**Packages shipped on dry ice must be marked with a\n   hazard label. The carrier generally will apply a dry ice surcharge. Also, most airlines have a\n   restriction on how much dry ice is allowed onboard while freighters may carry more than passenger\n   aircraft. Improper packaging of samples and restrictions on dry ice loading on airlines can lead\n   to samples stranded on the tarmac. This can ultimately result in a delay in providing healthcare\n   and increased cost in procuring another sample. Read more on how to mitigate this risk of delay\n   of frozen samples shipped on dry ice [Read more\u2026][16]\n2. **Freezing of refrigerated and controlled room temperature (CRT) samples**Refrigerated and CRT\n   samples can easily damage if frozen. Long exposure to winter ambient temperatures and freezing\n   temperatures in airline cargo sections can reduce the temperature of refrigerated samples well\n   below freezing. Read more on how to mitigate this risk of freezing samples [Read more\u2026][17]\n\n#### [Ice Packs][18]\n\nMaintain frozen payloads below -20\u00b0C (-4\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][19]\n\n#### [Freezer Packs][20]\n\nMaintain frozen payloads below -5\u00b0C (+23\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][21]\n\n#### [Cool Packs][22]\n\nMaintain refrigerated payloads below +8\u00b0C (+46\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][23]\n\n#### [CRT Packs][24]\n\nProvides freeze protection to CRT loads, maintaining temperature above +15\u00b0C (+59\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][25]\n\n#### [Ambient Packs][26]\n\nProvides overheat protection, maintaining temperature below +25\u00b0C (+77\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][27]\n\n### Need Help?\n\n[ Get in Touch ][28] [Up arrow]\n[ [PCM] ][29]\n* [Home][30]\n* [Industry Challenges][31]\n  * [Common Sample Type & Recommended Shipping][32]\n* [Resources][33]\n  * [Faq][34]\n  * [Blog][35]\n* [Products][36]\n  * [Cool Packs][37]\n  * [Ice Packs][38]\n  * [Freezer Packs][39]\n  * [CRT Packs][40]\n  * [Ambient Packs][41]\n* [Contact][42]\n* [ 170 Bradley Branch Rd Ste 9 Arden NC 28704 ][43]\n* [ Phone: (828) 708-7178 ][44]\n* [ Monday - Friday\n  8 AM - 5 PM EST ][45]\n* [ Email Us ][46]\n* [Contact][47]\n* [Terms & Conditions][48]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 RGEES, LLC. All Right Reserved.\n\n[1]: #primary\n[2]: https://pcmpacks.com/\n[3]: https://pcmpacks.com/\n[4]: https://pcmpacks.com/industry-challenges/\n[5]: https://pcmpacks.com/common-sample-type-recommended-shipping/\n[6]: https://pcmpacks.com/faq/\n[7]: https://pcmpacks.com/faq/\n[8]: https://pcmpacks.com/blog/\n[9]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[10]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[11]: https://pcmpacks.com/ice-packs/\n[12]: https://pcmpacks.com/freezer-packs/\n[13]: https://pcmpacks.com/crt-packs/\n[14]: https://pcmpacks.com/ambient-packs/\n[15]: https://pcmpacks.com/contact/\n[16]: https://pcmpacks.com/industry-challenges/\n[17]: https://pcmpacks.com/industry-challenges/\n[18]: https://pcmpacks.com/ice-packs/\n[19]: https://pcmpacks.com/ice-packs/\n[20]: https://pcmpacks.com/freezer-packs/\n[21]: https://pcmpacks.com/freezer-packs/\n[22]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[23]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[24]: https://pcmpacks.com/crt-packs/\n[25]: https://pcmpacks.com/crt-packs/\n[26]: https://pcmpacks.com/ambient-packs/\n[27]: https://pcmpacks.com/ambient-packs/\n[28]: /contact\n[29]: https://pcmpacks.com\n[30]: https://pcmpacks.com/\n[31]: https://pcmpacks.com/industry-challenges/\n[32]: https://pcmpacks.com/common-sample-type-recommended-shipping/\n[33]: https://pcmpacks.com/faq/\n[34]: https://pcmpacks.com/faq/\n[35]: https://pcmpacks.com/blog/\n[36]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[37]: https://pcmpacks.com/cool-packs/\n[38]: https://pcmpacks.com/ice-packs/\n[39]: https://pcmpacks.com/freezer-packs/\n[40]: https://pcmpacks.com/crt-packs/\n[41]: https://pcmpacks.com/ambient-packs/\n[42]: https://pcmpacks.com/contact/\n[43]: https://goo.gl/maps/xzdjyf3ECTCKGebt8\n[44]: tel:+1-828-708-7178\n[45]: #\n[46]: mailto:sales@akuratemp.com\n[47]: https://pcmpacks.com/contact/\n[48]: /wp-content/uploads/2023/05/Terms.pdf [Skip to content][1]\n[[PCM packs]][2] PHASE CHANGE MATERIAL\nToggle navigation\n* [Home][3]\n* [Industry Challenges][4]\n  * [Common Sample Type & Recommended Shipping][5]\n* [Resources][6]\n  * [Faq][7]\n  * [Blog][8]\n* [Products][9]\n  * [Cool Packs][10]\n  * [Ice Packs][11]\n  * [Freezer Packs][12]\n  * [CRT Packs][13]\n  * [Ambient Packs][14]\n* [Contact][15]\n\n\u00a0\n\nManufacturer for **savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs**, a sustainable series of phase change material based cold\nchain refrigerants.\n\nProtect your diagnostic and clinical trial samples from the risks of temperature excursion by\ntransporting them with **savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs**, a sustainable series of phase change material-based\ncold chain refrigerants.\n\n[home banner]\n\n# Reduce the risk of temperature excursions with savENRG\u00ae PCM Packs\n\n## **What happens when samples are exposed to extreme temperatures?**\n1. **Delay of frozen samples shipped on dry-ice**Packages shipped on dry ice must be marked with a\n   hazard label. The carrier generally will apply a dry ice surcharge. Also, most airlines have a\n   restriction on how much dry ice is allowed onboard while freighters may carry more than passenger\n   aircraft. Improper packaging of samples and restrictions on dry ice loading on airlines can lead\n   to samples stranded on the tarmac. This can ultimately result in a delay in providing healthcare\n   and increased cost in procuring another sample. Read more on how to mitigate this risk of delay\n   of frozen samples shipped on dry ice [Read more\u2026][16]\n2. **Freezing of refrigerated and controlled room temperature (CRT) samples**Refrigerated and CRT\n   samples can easily damage if frozen. Long exposure to winter ambient temperatures and freezing\n   temperatures in airline cargo sections can reduce the temperature of refrigerated samples well\n   below freezing. Read more on how to mitigate this risk of freezing samples [Read more\u2026][17]\n\n#### [Ice Packs][18]\n\nMaintain frozen payloads below -20\u00b0C (-4\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][19]\n\n#### [Freezer Packs][20]\n\nMaintain frozen payloads below -5\u00b0C (+23\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][21]\n\n#### [Cool Packs][22]\n\nMaintain refrigerated payloads below +8\u00b0C (+46\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][23]\n\n#### [CRT Packs][24]\n\nProvides freeze protection to CRT loads, maintaining temperature above +15\u00b0C (+59\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][25]\n\n#### [Ambient Packs][26]\n\nProvides overheat protection, maintaining temperature below +25\u00b0C (+77\u00b0F)\n\n[Read More...][27]\n\n### Need Help?\n\n[ Get in Touch ][28] [Up arrow]\n[ [PCM] ][29]\n* [Home][30]\n* [Industry Challenges][31]\n  * [Common Sample Type & Recommended Shipping][32]\n* [Resources][33]\n  * [Faq][34]\n  * [Blog][35]\n* [Products][36]\n  * [Cool Packs][37]\n  * [Ice Packs][38]\n  * [Freezer Packs][39]\n  * [CRT Packs][40]\n  * [Ambient Packs][41]\n* [Contact][42]\n* [ 170 Bradley Branch Rd Ste 9