ap and needs.\n\nFor those recovering from recent surgery or looking extra cold therapy, consider the **[ActiveWrap\u00ae\nLong Duration Ice Packs][285]**. The long duration ice packs deliver two to four hours (depending on\nsize) of flexible, ice-cold pain relief and designed for use over post-surgical bandages. The Long\nDuration Ice Packs only deliver cold therapy, for both hot and cold therapy select the Ultra Flex\npacks.\n\n## SIZING\n* Small (4.5\" x 6.5\"): for wrist & foot wraps\n* Medium (6\" x 9\"): ankle, elbow & neck wraps\n* Large (7\" X 10\"): knee & shoulder wraps\n* Large Square (10\" X 10\"): hip & back wraps\n* X-Large (13.5\" x 10\"): XXL back & hip wraps\n\n## How to use\n\n**For Cold Therapy:**\n1. Place the pack in the freezer for at least two hours.\n2. Insert the frozen pack into the included nylon dual pocket pouch. [See video here][286]\n3. Attach the pack to the inside of your wrap.\n4. Use for up to 15 minutes or as directed by your medical care provider.\n5. Remove and allow skin to return to normal temperature before reapplying.\n\n**For Heat Therapy: **[Click here for video demo][287]\n1. Follow instructions on pack (heat time varies with pack size).\n2. Insert the heated pack into the included nylon pouch.\n3. Attached the pack to the inside of your wrap.\n4. Use for up to 20 minutes or"
