            "text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[ [Insulated Products Corporation] ][2]\n[ Menu ][3]\n* [Products][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [One-Piece Box Liners][6]\n* [SustainaLiner: 24 hrs ][7]\n* [CooLiner Box Liner: 24 hrs][8]\n* [BROWSE PRODUCTS BY FEATURE][9]\n* [Multi-Piece Box Liners][10]\n* [CelluLiner Paper Box Liner: 48 hrs+][11]\n* [PopupLiner 2-Piece: 48 hrs+][12]\n* [Pouch/Mailer Insulation][13]\n* [Paper Pouch: 48 hrs+][14]\n* [PopupLiner Pouch: 48 hrs+][15]\n* [CooLiner Pouch: 24 hrs][16]\n* [AerVault Mailers: 48 hrs][17]\n* [CryoVault Pouch: 48 hrs][18]\n* [Delivery][19]\n* [Paper Insulated Delivery Bag][20]\n* [Paper Grocery Delivery Bag][21]\n* [Bubble Insulated Delivery Bag][22]\n* [Paper Insulated Roll][23]\n* [Large Cargo][24]\n* [Foil Insulation Roll][25]\n* [Insulated Cargo Blankets][26]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][27]\n* [Air Cargo Insulation][28]\n* [Cold Gel Packs][29]\n* [Gel Packs][30]\n* [Sweat-Proof Gel Packs][31]\n* [Drain-Friendly Gel Packs][32]\n* [Super-Absorbent Polymer for Gel Packs][33]\n* [Foam Bricks][34]\n* [Industries][35]\n* [Cold Chain Packaging][36]\n* [Food][37]\n* [Meat][38]\n* [Pharmaceuticals][39]\n* [Vaccines][40]\n* [Direct to Consumer][41]\n* [Company][42]\n* [Company][43]\n* [Our Materials][44]\n* [Performance Testing][45]\n* [Ordering and Distribution][46]\n* [Sustainably Engineered][47]\n* [FAQ][48]\n* [Resources][49]\n* [Knowledge Base][50]\n* [FAQ][51]\n* [General FAQ][52]\n* [Shipping Regulations][53]\n* [How To Ship Refrigerated Products][54]\n* [How to Ship Frozen Products][55]\n* [Shipping Perishables: Tips and Guidance][56]\n* [Shipping With Cold Packs vs. Dry Ice][57]\n* [Industry Applications][58]\n* [How to Ship Meat][59]\n* [How to Ship Chocolate][60]\n* [How to Ship Ice Cream][61]\n* [Product FAQ][62]\n* [Custom Sized Insulated Packaging][63]\n* [Case Studies][64]\n* [Pharmaceuticals Case Studies][65]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Pharmaceuticals | IPC][66]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Medicines & Pharmaceuticals | IPC][67]\n* [Food Case Studies][68]\n* [Expanding Reach for Mail-Order Beef with Insulated Shipping | IPC][69]\n* [Shipping Multiple Product Types Inside Single Container | IPC][70]\n* [How to Keep Ice Cream from Melting \u2013 Eco Insulated Pouch | IPC][71]\n* [Distributor Case Studies][72]\n* [Eliminating the Need for Refrigerated Trucking | IPC][73]\n* [White Papers][74]\n* [Pharmaceutical White Papers][75]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][76]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][77]\n* [2-8 \u00b0C Temperature Protection During Shipping | IPC][78]\n* [Shipment of Refrigerated Medical Vials Using PCM and PopupLiner Box Liner \u2013 Insulated\nProducts Corporation][79]\n* [Temperature-Controlled Packaging for Reusable Containers Using IPC\u2019s PopupLiner Thermal Box\nLiner \u2013 Insulated Products Corporation][80]\n* [Food White Papers][81]\n* [Insulation Solutions for Frozen Food Shipping | IPC][82]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][83]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][84]\n* [Beverage White Papers][85]\n* [48-hour Thermal Protection for Shipping Wine | IPC][86]\n* [Shipping Frozen Human Milk Using Insulated Containers | IPC][87]\n* [Industrial White Papers][88]\n* [Freeze Protection when Shipping Water-based Paint & Grout | IPC][89]\n* [Insights][90]\n* [Jobs][91]\n* [Contact][92]\n* [Request Quote][93]\n* [Shipping Guides][94]\n[Close Search ][95]\n\n# Insulated Cargo Blankets\n\nCold weather protection for freight\n\n[Slide] \"IPC's CooLiner provides excellent isolation\" [Slide] \"The consistency and quality has been\nkey to our large-quantity transport success\" JOHN, DUPONT CORP\n[Play Video][96]\n\nThe most effective, affordable and flexible way to protect your temperature-sensitive freight.\n\n[Insulated Cargo Blankets]\n\nOur Insulated Cargo Blankets are the ideal one-way solution for shielding your perishable and\ntemperature-sensitive goods against extreme ambient temperatures throughout the cold-chain shipping\nprocess.\n\nA combination of advanced durability and the innovative use of \u201cspace-age\u201d reflective insulation\ntechnology sets IPC\u2019s recyclable #7* insulated cargo blankets apart from other thermal packaging\nalternatives. With IPC products, you\u2019ll always know your goods are protected, regardless of the\nseason or distance traveled.\n\nThermal cargo blankets are widely used worldwide to protect solids and liquids such as medical\nfluids, pharmaceutical components, water-based paints, industrial chemicals, seafood, and meat. Our\nsturdy and tear-proof insulated blankets are a high-performance method of insulating bulk quantities\nof goods for as long as six days, yet they are priced at a fraction of the cost of re-useable\ncovers.\n\n**May not be recyclable in your area*\n\n[Request a Quote][97] [View Brochure][98]\n\n### [Learn more about how our insulated cargo blankets provide effective temperature control.][99]\n\nOur lightweight insulated cargo blankets work perfectly as bubble blankets for pallets. They deliver\noutstanding temperature-control performance, fulfilling the need for large-format thermal protection\nfor less than the cost of container-load insulated shipping covers. CooLiner insulated cargo\nblankets, our premier insulation line for pallet-sized goods, are also helpful in instances where\ncombined loads of multiple-temperature goods are shipped inside a single trailer, providing\nprotection against both cold and heat.\n\nThe low-cost blankets for pallets provide high-performance temperature control and are appropriate\nfor a variety of different product applications. They also save space, arriving folded, and are easy\nto apply, helping to minimize labor costs.\n\nAs a worldwide leader and innovator in the development and manufacturing of cold chain thermal\npackaging, IPC provides high-performance insulation products to fit your specific needs and\nrequirements. Our choice of insulation materials, solid manufacturing processes, and the unique\ndesign of our finished products all contribute to the net result: unparalleled performance against\ncold and heat for your valuable goods, priced affordably.\n\n### CooLiner Cargo Blanket\n\n[ [Thermal Pallet Cover] ][100]\n\nThe most popular cargo cover in our selection.\n\n### EcoBlanket Extreme\n\n[ [Insulating Pallet Covers] ][101]\n\nFor more powerful protection against the most extreme ambient temperatures.\n\n## Available in Various Thickness\n\nOur Insulated Cargo Blanets are available in various levels of thickness that are offered depending\non your performance requirements.\n\n#### Lite\n\nMore streamlined for reduced costs.\n\n[CooLiner Lite]\n\n#### Single Bubble\n\nSuitable for shiments lasting 24 hours.\n\n#### Double Bubble\n\nDual bubble layer provides 20% better protection.\n\n[CooLiner Double Bubble Diagram]\n\n## What makes our Insulated Cargo Blankets superior?\n* **Effective protection against extreme temperatures.\n**The insulating covers ensure protection of your cargo against extreme cold and heat.\n* **Preventing against radiation, conduction and convection.\n**The innovative insulated bubble wrap protects against all types of heat transfer.\n* **Lightweight and flexible**.\nThe durable insulation blankets can be stored, transported and used easily.\n* **Minimizing your costs.\n**Our Insulated Cargo Blankets are a low-cost shipping solution that saves you money by minimizing\nspoilage, while also reducing storage and shipping costs.\n\n#### Available in custom sizes\n\nOur in-house manufacturing facility allows us to make fully customizable sizes to suit your exact\nrequirements, and we do this at no additional cost. Get in touch for more information.\n\n[Request a Quote][102] [View Brochure][103]\n\n[ [Blanket Insulation] ][104]\n\n### Extreme EcoBlanket Roll\n\nExtreme EcoBlanket rolls are thermal blankets designed to protect individual pallets of\ntemperature-sensitive products from excessive exposure to heat and cold. Consider Extreme EcoBlanket\na viable alternative to refrigerated carriers or reefer trucks; one that can be used to prevent\ndrums, totes, pallets, and other commodities from deterioration due to excessive heat and cold\ntemperatures.\n\nThe triple-layered insulated blankets combine dual-sided, ultra-radiant barrier film that retards\nthermal radiation, and a super-insulating textile layer with a thickness of around 1\u201d that\nsignificantly slows down the rate of thermal conduction. In addition to superior performance, IPC\u2019s\nEcoBlanket comprises mostly natural fibers, leading to a reduced negative impact on human health and\nthe environment when compared with competing products.\n\n[ [Cargo Blankets] ][105]\n[ [Insulated Blankets] ][106]\n[ [Insulated Cargo Blanket Covers] ][107]\n\nCooLiner Cargo Blankets keep your warm freight protected against extremely cold ambient temperatures\n\n### Protect your shipments against extreme cold temperatures this winter.\n\nOur Insulated Cargo Covers protect your shipments against the extreme cold of winter for up to six\ndays. Constructed with a dual-layered temperature-protection technology, the CooLiner material lets\nyou rest assured your goods will reach their destination without spoilage.\n* Place the lightweight CooLiner insulated blanket over your temperature-sensitive cargo and seal\n* The ultra-radiant barrier and insulating foam effectively prevent conductive, convective and\nradiative heat transfer\n* External cold is unable to penetrate the blanket insulation cover, keeping shipments at a\ncontrolled temperature\n* Save money on handling, storage and spoilage\n\n## Proven Performance\n\nThe performance of the CooLiner cargo covers was tested in our in-house environmental testing\nchamber to ensure they would effectively protect cargo during transit. As demonstrated by the graphs\nbelow, the CooLiner thermal blanket provided effective temperature control for over six days in both\nextreme heat and cold.\n\n## Frequently\n## Asked\n## Questions\n\n### [What is CooLiner material?][108]\n\nCooLiner is a revolutionary type of insulation material that protects temperature-sensitive\nshipments for 24 hours against extreme high and low temperatures. The high degree of temperature\ncontrol is achieved through the combination of internal air bubbles and reflective metalized films,\ncreating a thermal silver bubble wrap.\n\nThe CooLiner thermal blankets are very straightforward to use. Simply position the cargo blankets\nover your shipment, drape over the front and sides of the goods. Your freight is now protected.\n\n### [How does CooLiner work?][109]\n\nMany years of dedication to developing superior new products resulted in the conception of the\nCooLiner insulated cargo covers, and this proprietary technology is not available anywhere else.\n\nThe most important aspect of CooLiner, with respect to providing effective temperature control, is\nthe material\u2019s low mass combined with a highly reflective outer layer. The low-mass bubble layer\nrestricts conductive heat transfer, while the outer layer prevents heat from radiating from the\nambient air.\n\nCrafted over 12 years of continual development, IPC CooLiner technology provides tried-and-tested,\nreal-world efficacy.\n\nIn cargo cover format, the material provides effective protection in that it reflects heat radiating\nfrom above, more efficiently than heat approaching from the sides.\n\n### [What makes CooLiner superior?][110]\n* CooLiner will effectively keep your shipments within the predefined temperature range during the\ntransit duration. We make sure of this in our in-house testing lab.\n* It features a space-saving design that allows more efficient folding and storage.\n* The material is durably constructed to resists damage.\n* A waterproof outer layer prevents leaks\n* The single-use cargo blanket can be easily and cheaply disposed of after use.\n\n### [How does CooLiner save me money?][111]\n\nThe key benefit provided by CooLiner material over other similar products comes down to efficiency\nand savings.\n\nThe space-saving design of CooLiner allows efficient use throughout the entire packaging process.\nFrom storage to packaging, the foldable nature of CooLiner helps to kee"
