            "text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[ [Insulated Products Corporation] ][2]\n[ Menu ][3]\n* [Products][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [One-Piece Box Liners][6]\n* [SustainaLiner: 24 hrs ][7]\n* [CooLiner Box Liner: 24 hrs][8]\n* [BROWSE PRODUCTS BY FEATURE][9]\n* [Multi-Piece Box Liners][10]\n* [CelluLiner Paper Box Liner: 48 hrs+][11]\n* [PopupLiner 2-Piece: 48 hrs+][12]\n* [Pouch/Mailer Insulation][13]\n* [Paper Pouch: 48 hrs+][14]\n* [PopupLiner Pouch: 48 hrs+][15]\n* [CooLiner Pouch: 24 hrs][16]\n* [AerVault Mailers: 48 hrs][17]\n* [CryoVault Pouch: 48 hrs][18]\n* [Delivery][19]\n* [Paper Insulated Delivery Bag][20]\n* [Paper Grocery Delivery Bag][21]\n* [Bubble Insulated Delivery Bag][22]\n* [Paper Insulated Roll][23]\n* [Large Cargo][24]\n* [Foil Insulation Roll][25]\n* [Insulated Cargo Blankets][26]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][27]\n* [Air Cargo Insulation][28]\n* [Cold Gel Packs][29]\n* [Gel Packs][30]\n* [Sweat-Proof Gel Packs][31]\n* [Drain-Friendly Gel Packs][32]\n* [Super-Absorbent Polymer for Gel Packs][33]\n* [Foam Bricks][34]\n* [Industries][35]\n* [Cold Chain Packaging][36]\n* [Food][37]\n* [Meat][38]\n* [Pharmaceuticals][39]\n* [Vaccines][40]\n* [Direct to Consumer][41]\n* [Company][42]\n* [Company][43]\n* [Our Materials][44]\n* [Performance Testing][45]\n* [Ordering and Distribution][46]\n* [Sustainably Engineered][47]\n* [FAQ][48]\n* [Resources][49]\n* [Knowledge Base][50]\n* [FAQ][51]\n* [General FAQ][52]\n* [Shipping Regulations][53]\n* [How To Ship Refrigerated Products][54]\n* [How to Ship Frozen Products][55]\n* [Shipping Perishables: Tips and Guidance][56]\n* [Shipping With Cold Packs vs. Dry Ice][57]\n* [Industry Applications][58]\n* [How to Ship Meat][59]\n* [How to Ship Chocolate][60]\n* [How to Ship Ice Cream][61]\n* [Product FAQ][62]\n* [Custom Sized Insulated Packaging][63]\n* [Case Studies][64]\n* [Pharmaceuticals Case Studies][65]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Pharmaceuticals | IPC][66]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Medicines & Pharmaceuticals | IPC][67]\n* [Food Case Studies][68]\n* [Expanding Reach for Mail-Order Beef with Insulated Shipping | IPC][69]\n* [Shipping Multiple Product Types Inside Single Container | IPC][70]\n* [How to Keep Ice Cream from Melting \u2013 Eco Insulated Pouch | IPC][71]\n* [Distributor Case Studies][72]\n* [Eliminating the Need for Refrigerated Trucking | IPC][73]\n* [White Papers][74]\n* [Pharmaceutical White Papers][75]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][76]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][77]\n* [2-8 \u00b0C Temperature Protection During Shipping | IPC][78]\n* [Shipment of Refrigerated Medical Vials Using PCM and PopupLiner Box Liner \u2013 Insulated\nProducts Corporation][79]\n* [Temperature-Controlled Packaging for Reusable Containers Using IPC\u2019s PopupLiner Thermal Box\nLiner \u2013 Insulated Products Corporation][80]\n* [Food White Papers][81]\n* [Insulation Solutions for Frozen Food Shipping | IPC][82]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][83]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][84]\n* [Beverage White Papers][85]\n* [48-hour Thermal Protection for Shipping Wine | IPC][86]\n* [Shipping Frozen Human Milk Using Insulated Containers | IPC][87]\n* [Industrial White Papers][88]\n* [Freeze Protection when Shipping Water-based Paint & Grout | IPC][89]\n* [Insights][90]\n* [Jobs][91]\n* [Contact][92]\n* [Request Quote][93]\n* [Shipping Guides][94]\n[Close Search ][95]\n\n# Insulated Pallet Covers\n\n[Slide] \"IPC's CooLiner provides excellent isolation\" [Slide] \"The consistency and quality has been\nkey to our large-quantity transport success\" JOHN, DUPONT CORP\n\n### The perfect solution for insulating pallet shipments for more than 24 hours.\n\nOur Insulated Pallet Covers protect against extreme ambient temperatures for more than 24 hours.\n\nManufactured using our innovative and recyclable #7* CooLiner material, these lightweight Pallet\nCovers can be quickly and easily applied to shipments, protecting them against damaging temperature\nexcursions during transit.\n\nWhile providing high-performance temperature control, CooLiner is an extremely cost-effective\nsolution when compared to refrigerated trucking. The insulating blankets also help prevent heat\ndamage in cross-dock shipping and on the tarmac.\n\nThe dual-layered material combines an ultra-radiant barrier and a super-insulating bubble layer.\nThis provides the strength and flexibility needed to resist punctures and withstand rigorous\nhandling during transit, while also blocking light, UV and odor transfer.\n\n**May not be recyclable in your area*\n\n#### Custom sizes and minimum order quantities\n\nWe specialize in manufacturing custom sizes to suit your exact requirements, and we do this at no\nextra cost. Get in touch with us to discuss your requirements.\n\nThe minimum order quantity for Insulated Pallet Covers is 500 sets/pcs per size. Learn more about\nour [minimum order quantities][96] here.\n\n[Request a Quote][97] [View Brochure][98]\n\n### [Read more about our Insulated Pallet Cover][99]\n\n**High-Performance Insulation**\n\nThe innovative pallet covers are constructed with our proprietary foil bubble material, and provide\nprotection against extreme hot and cold temperatures. We assist our clients in keeping bulk\nshipments at consistent temperatures throughout the transit duration.\n\nThe thermal pallet covers provide you with the most cost-effective temperature control for\nless-than-container-load shipments.\n\n**Custom Manufacturing**\n\nWe specialize in manufacturing custom sizes of insulated covers for our clients, tailor-made to\n\u201cfit\u201d the needs of the client.\n\nAlthough the insulated pallet blankets provide an extremely high level of temperature-control\nperformance, they are priced at a fraction of the price of reusable covers. CooLiner insulated\ncovers are generally one-use, disposable products, meaning no reverse logistics are required.\n\n**Insulating Bulk Shipments**\n\nCooLiner insulation blankets provide an excellent method of insulating bulk quantities of goods. The\npallet covers deliver outstanding temperature-control performance against cold and heat. They are\nwidely used in the United States and worldwide to protect solids and liquid products, including\nmedical fluids, pharmaceutical components, water-based paints, industrial chemicals,\ntemperature-sensitive industrial materials, seafood, and meat.\n\nThe insulated bubble wraps can be used as insulated shrouds & insulated hoods, and are among the\nmost cost-effective types of thermal pallet protection products available.\n\nIn addition to temp-shield temperature-control shipping materials like the CooLiner thermal blanket\ncover, IPC also manufactures kits to protect [Air Cargo][100] LD3, LD8 and LD 10 containers.\n\n## Available in Various Thickness\n\nOur Insulated Pallet Covers are available in various levels of thickness that are offered depending\non your performance requirements.\n\n#### Lite\n\nMore streamlined for reduced costs.\n\n[CooLiner Lite]\n\n#### Single Bubble\n\nSuitable for shiments lasting 24 hours.\n\n#### Double Bubble\n\nDual bubble layer provides 20% better protection.\n\n[CooLiner Double Bubble Diagram]\n[ [Insulated Pallet Blankets] ][101]\n\n## Features\n* ##### Sturdy, tear-proof, heat-sealed, foil bubble material.\n* ##### Arrives folded with space-saving design.\n* ##### Quick and easy to apply, saving on labor.\n* ##### Collapsible and easy to dispose of.\n* ##### Low cost, single-use design; no reverse logistics required.\n* Reusable with some applications.\n* ##### Provides high level of light, solar radiation and UV protection.\n* ##### Made of reflective radiant barrier materials\n* ##### Peel-and-seal self-adhesive easy closure\n\n##### **Watch the video below to see how to insulate your shipments using CooLiner pallet\n##### insulation.**\n\n## Insulated Cargo Blankets\n\nBe sure to take a look at our [Insulated Cargo Blankets][102], which are made from the same\nhigh-performance material as our Insulated Pallet Covers. The cargo blankets are suitable for larger\nshipments as they allow you to protect an entire container against extreme temperatures in a matter\nof seconds.\n\n[View Insulated Cargo Blankets][103]\n[ [Insulated Cargo Blankets] ][104]\n\n### What Makes Our Insulated Pallet Covers Superior?\n* ##### Protection Against Extreme Cold and Heat\n\nRecommended for protection of room temperature or refrigerated products against cold and heat\nextremes.\n* ##### Extreme Space Efficiency\n\nThermal pallet covers arrive compact and compressed for easy storage and transportation.\n* ##### Made of Robust, Durable Material\n\nOur thermal pallet covers are made using sturdy, puncture-resistant, heat-sealed, foil-bubble\nmaterial.\n* ##### Easy to Use\n\nEasy-to-use design allows you to apply your insulated pallet cover in seconds using a\npeel-and-seal adhesive closure.\n\n[ [Insulated Pallet Cover] ][105]\n\n## Performance Testing\n\n## Frequently\n## Asked\n## Questions\n\n### [How is CooLiner material used in a pallet cover format?][106]\n\nMade from air bubbles encased inside metalized films, CooLiner pallet covers are an effective type\nof insulated packaging that protect shipments against temperature extremes.\n\nThe insulated pallet blankets could not be easier to use, and are available in any custom size.\nSimply position the insulation over your pallet-sized shipment, pull down and over, reveal the\nadhesive peel and seal closure, and seal and secure the pallet.\n\n### [How does CooLiner work?][107]\n\nYears of research at IPC resulted in development of the advanced CooLiner insulation material, which\nis not available to others in the industry. The material combines a low mass with a highly\nreflective outer layer to achieve high-performance temperature control.\n\nThe reflective foil insulation layer, covering the entire exterior of the pallet, prevents heat from\nradiating into the product.\n\nThe high level of temperature control is achieved using a unique, low-mass bubble structure that\ninhibits conductive heat transfer. It is important to use the appropriate weight (gauge) for this\napplication. While thicker, heavier films are more durable, they have a higher level of thermal mass\nthat can enhance heat flow.\n\nThe result of 11 years of meticulous research, IPC\u2019s advanced bubble insulation technology provides\nreal-world efficacy.\n\n### [What makes CooLiner superior?][108]\n\nCooLiner silver bubble wrap is superior to other available products for the following reasons:\n* It offers a highly effective, reliable form of insulated packaging.\n* It features a space-saving design for more efficient storage.\n* The robust material will not tear or puncture while in transit.\n* A waterproof design prevents any leaks from occurring.\n* It can be easily disposed of.\n\n### [How does CooLiner save me money?][109]\n\nThe key advantage provided by CooLiner over other similar products in the market is the money-saving\npotential. It all comes down to efficiency.\n\nCooLiner features a space-saving design that allows it to be efficiently folded and stored when not\nin use. The feature also provides more efficiency in the pack area in that less work is involved in\nmoving it through the packaging process.\n\nBusinesses using CooLiner products can also benefit from their ease of use. The insulation can be\napplied to your pallet in seconds. Simple position it over your pallet shipment, and seal using the\npeel-and-seal adhesive tape.\n\n### [How can foil bubble insulated pallet covers help protect PLA plastic items from warping during\n### shipment?][110]\n\nPLA (polylactic acid) plastics can soften or deform at temperatures above 60 \u00b0C (140 \u00b0F), making\ntemperature protection critical during transit or storage. IPC\u2019s foil bubble insulated pallet covers\nreflect radiant heat and reduce temperature spikes inside the load, helping maintain the shape and\nstructural integrity of PLA-based products even in hot shipping conditions. For sensitive shipments,\nwe can pair covers with phase change materials or gel packs to stabilize internal temperatures\nfurther.\n\n**All our products are developed and manufactured from our factory in the USA.*"
