            "text": "[Skip to main content][1]\n[ [Insulated Products Corporation] ][2]\n[ Menu ][3]\n* [Products][4]\n* [Products][5]\n* [One-Piece Box Liners][6]\n* [SustainaLiner: 24 hrs ][7]\n* [CooLiner Box Liner: 24 hrs][8]\n* [BROWSE PRODUCTS BY FEATURE][9]\n* [Multi-Piece Box Liners][10]\n* [CelluLiner Paper Box Liner: 48 hrs+][11]\n* [PopupLiner 2-Piece: 48 hrs+][12]\n* [Pouch/Mailer Insulation][13]\n* [Paper Pouch: 48 hrs+][14]\n* [PopupLiner Pouch: 48 hrs+][15]\n* [CooLiner Pouch: 24 hrs][16]\n* [AerVault Mailers: 48 hrs][17]\n* [CryoVault Pouch: 48 hrs][18]\n* [Delivery][19]\n* [Paper Insulated Delivery Bag][20]\n* [Paper Grocery Delivery Bag][21]\n* [Bubble Insulated Delivery Bag][22]\n* [Paper Insulated Roll][23]\n* [Large Cargo][24]\n* [Foil Insulation Roll][25]\n* [Insulated Cargo Blankets][26]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][27]\n* [Air Cargo Insulation][28]\n* [Cold Gel Packs][29]\n* [Gel Packs][30]\n* [Sweat-Proof Gel Packs][31]\n* [Drain-Friendly Gel Packs][32]\n* [Super-Absorbent Polymer for Gel Packs][33]\n* [Foam Bricks][34]\n* [Industries][35]\n* [Cold Chain Packaging][36]\n* [Food][37]\n* [Meat][38]\n* [Pharmaceuticals][39]\n* [Vaccines][40]\n* [Direct to Consumer][41]\n* [Company][42]\n* [Company][43]\n* [Our Materials][44]\n* [Performance Testing][45]\n* [Ordering and Distribution][46]\n* [Sustainably Engineered][47]\n* [FAQ][48]\n* [Resources][49]\n* [Knowledge Base][50]\n* [FAQ][51]\n* [General FAQ][52]\n* [Shipping Regulations][53]\n* [How To Ship Refrigerated Products][54]\n* [How to Ship Frozen Products][55]\n* [Shipping Perishables: Tips and Guidance][56]\n* [Shipping With Cold Packs vs. Dry Ice][57]\n* [Industry Applications][58]\n* [How to Ship Meat][59]\n* [How to Ship Chocolate][60]\n* [How to Ship Ice Cream][61]\n* [Product FAQ][62]\n* [Custom Sized Insulated Packaging][63]\n* [Case Studies][64]\n* [Pharmaceuticals Case Studies][65]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Pharmaceuticals | IPC][66]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Medicines & Pharmaceuticals | IPC][67]\n* [Food Case Studies][68]\n* [Expanding Reach for Mail-Order Beef with Insulated Shipping | IPC][69]\n* [Shipping Multiple Product Types Inside Single Container | IPC][70]\n* [How to Keep Ice Cream from Melting \u2013 Eco Insulated Pouch | IPC][71]\n* [Distributor Case Studies][72]\n* [Eliminating the Need for Refrigerated Trucking | IPC][73]\n* [White Papers][74]\n* [Pharmaceutical White Papers][75]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][76]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][77]\n* [2-8 \u00b0C Temperature Protection During Shipping | IPC][78]\n* [Shipment of Refrigerated Medical Vials Using PCM and PopupLiner Box Liner \u2013 Insulated\nProducts Corporation][79]\n* [Temperature-Controlled Packaging for Reusable Containers Using IPC\u2019s PopupLiner Thermal Box\nLiner \u2013 Insulated Products Corporation][80]\n* [Food White Papers][81]\n* [Insulation Solutions for Frozen Food Shipping | IPC][82]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][83]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][84]\n* [Beverage White Papers][85]\n* [48-hour Thermal Protection for Shipping Wine | IPC][86]\n* [Shipping Frozen Human Milk Using Insulated Containers | IPC][87]\n* [Industrial White Papers][88]\n* [Freeze Protection when Shipping Water-based Paint & Grout | IPC][89]\n* [Insights][90]\n* [Jobs][91]\n* [Contact][92]\n* [Request Quote][93]\n* [Shipping Guides][94]\n[Close Search ][95]\n\n# Super Absorbent Polymer for Manufacturing Gel Packs\n\n#### Bulk super-absorbent polymer powder that provides a cost-efficient method of manufacturing your\n#### own gel packs.\n\nIPC offers 50lb cases or supersacks of superabsorbent polymer (SAP) powder for manufacturing gel\npacks at low cost.\n\nWhether you are a gel pack manufacturer or ship temperature-sensitive products requiring gel packs,\nIPC\u2019s large payload of super absorbent gel crystal can save your business money compared to buying\ngel packs individually.\n\nSimply combine the super absorbent gel chemical with the appropriate volume of water and, with\nlittle to no agitation, create your own gel pack contents for maintaining hot or cold temperatures\nfor extended durations.\n\n[Request a Quote][96]\n[Super-Absorbent Polymer for Manufacturing Gel Packs]\n\n## Features\n* Large volume cases and sacks allow for low-cost gel pack manufacturing at scale.\n* Excellent water absorption and retention capacity for maximum thermal performance.\n* Non-toxic and environmentally friendly.\n* Straightforward to mix with water, requires little to no agitation.\n* Maintains water-retention properties even under moderate levels of vibration and pressure. Ideal\nfor deliveries.\n\n## Available in supersacks\n\nIPC provides super-absorbent polymer powder in bulk super sacks that allow you to achieve optimal\ncost-efficiency when manufacturing gel packs in-house.\n\n[super absorbent polymer for gel packs]\n\n## FAQs\n\n**How do SAPs help maintain particular temperature ranges when used in gel packs?**\n\nSuperabsorbent polymers retain up to 1,000 times their mass in water. Thanks to SAPs incredible\nabsorption capacity and water\u2019s insulating properties, SAP gel packs help maintain cold temperatures\nfor long periods after being frozen.\n\n**Can SAPs absorb other liquids?**\n\nNo, SAPs absorb water through hydrogen bonding.\n\n**Can SAP gel packs be recycled?**\n\nThe SAP gel pack contents have no recycling value but since they are non-toxic, they can be disposed\nof down the drain.\n\nThe outer shell of our [gel packs][97] can, however, be recycled.\n\n**How much SAPs do I need to make a gel pack?**\n\nSAPs can absorb up to 800 times its weight in distilled water, but only around 300 times its weight\nin tap water due to the presence of impurities such as calcium, sodium, and other mineral salts.\n\nNevertheless, this means one gram of SAPs is sufficient for one gel pack. And with IPC\u2019s 50lb case\nor supersack offerings, you can manufacture large quantities of gel packs at a low cost.\n\n**Are SAP gel packs safe?**\n\nSAPs are inert which means they have low reactivity. They have been rigorously tested and show\nextremely low toxicity for direct skin contact.\n\nThe US Food and Drug Administration also approved the use of SAPs for indirect contact with food,\nbut it is not safe to consume SAPs.\n\n## Gel Packs for Shipping\n\nAs well as supplying super-absorbent polymer for manufacturing [ice packs for shipping][98], we can\nalso provide ready-made gel packs to suit various different needs.\n\n[Drain-Friendly Gel Packs]\n\n#### **Drain-Friendly**\n\nNon-toxic and easy to dispose of in running water. Perfect for longer duration shipments with the\nneed for easy disposal after use.\n\n[Cold Packs for Shipping]\n\n#### **Consumer**\n\nOur consumer-grade cold packs are printed with safety labelling to ensure safe use.\n\n[Gel Ice Packs]\n\n#### **Sweat-Proof**\n\nBuilt with an advanced, layered exterior that minimizes condensation.\n\n[Cold Packs for Shipping]\n\n#### **Blue Industrial**\n\nMade with a tough, recyclable polyethylene plastic that is proven to be puncture-resistant and\nresist tears during rigorous handling.\n\n[Gel Packs for Shipping]\n\n#### **Custom-Printed**\n\nHave your logo custom-printed onto your gel packs, ensuring complete consistency with your branding.\n\n**All our products are developed and manufactured from our factory in the USA.**\n\nRequest a Quote\nRequest A Custom Sample\n\n[View plain text version of our spec sheet here.][99]\n\n### Want to know more about our paper square-bottom bags?\n\nCall us, we are here to help:\n\n# 310 638 0900\n\n[REQUEST A QUOTE][100]\n[Insulated Products Corp]\n\nIPC provides advanced temperature-sensitive packaging solutions for shipping, crafted using many\nyears of industry experience.\n\nCustom-sized manufacturing and proprietary technology are what make IPC different.\n\n[PMMI]\n\n#### Popular Products\n* [Insulated Box Liners][101]\n* [Insulated Delivery Bags][102]\n* [Insulated Cargo Blankets][103]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][104]\n* [Insulated Pouches][105]\n* [Gel Packs][106]\n\n#### USEFUL LINKS\n* [Products][107]\n* [New Innovations][108]\n* [Company][109]\n* [Performance Testing][110]\n* [Resources][111]\n* [Request a Quote][112]\n* [Jobs][113]\n* [Accessibility][114]\n\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n250 W. Artesia Blvd\nRancho Dominguez CA 90220\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[310-638-0900][115]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n[[email protected]][116]\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\n\n\u00a9 2026 Insulated Products Corporation\n* [twitter][117]\n* [facebook][118]\n* [linkedin][119]\n* [youtube][120]\n\n[Close Menu ][121]\n\n* [Products][122]\n* [Products][123]\n* [One-Piece Box Liners][124]\n* [SustainaLiner: 24 hrs ][125]\n* [CooLiner Box Liner: 24 hrs][126]\n* [BROWSE PRODUCTS BY FEATURE][127]\n* [Multi-Piece Box Liners][128]\n* [CelluLiner Paper Box Liner: 48 hrs+][129]\n* [PopupLiner 2-Piece: 48 hrs+][130]\n* [Pouch/Mailer Insulation][131]\n* [Paper Pouch: 48 hrs+][132]\n* [PopupLiner Pouch: 48 hrs+][133]\n* [CooLiner Pouch: 24 hrs][134]\n* [AerVault Mailers: 48 hrs][135]\n* [CryoVault Pouch: 48 hrs][136]\n* [Delivery][137]\n* [Paper Insulated Delivery Bag][138]\n* [Paper Grocery Delivery Bag][139]\n* [Bubble Insulated Delivery Bag][140]\n* [Paper Insulated Roll][141]\n* [Large Cargo][142]\n* [Foil Insulation Roll][143]\n* [Insulated Cargo Blankets][144]\n* [Insulated Pallet Covers][145]\n* [Air Cargo Insulation][146]\n* [Cold Gel Packs][147]\n* [Gel Packs][148]\n* [Sweat-Proof Gel Packs][149]\n* [Drain-Friendly Gel Packs][150]\n* [Super-Absorbent Polymer for Gel Packs][151]\n* [Foam Bricks][152]\n* [Industries][153]\n* [Cold Chain Packaging][154]\n* [Food][155]\n* [Meat][156]\n* [Pharmaceuticals][157]\n* [Vaccines][158]\n* [Direct to Consumer][159]\n* [Company][160]\n* [Company][161]\n* [Our Materials][162]\n* [Performance Testing][163]\n* [Ordering and Distribution][164]\n* [Sustainably Engineered][165]\n* [FAQ][166]\n* [Resources][167]\n* [Knowledge Base][168]\n* [FAQ][169]\n* [General FAQ][170]\n* [Shipping Regulations][171]\n* [How To Ship Refrigerated Products][172]\n* [How to Ship Frozen Products][173]\n* [Shipping Perishables: Tips and Guidance][174]\n* [Shipping With Cold Packs vs. Dry Ice][175]\n* [Industry Applications][176]\n* [How to Ship Meat][177]\n* [How to Ship Chocolate][178]\n* [How to Ship Ice Cream][179]\n* [Product FAQ][180]\n* [Custom Sized Insulated Packaging][181]\n* [Case Studies][182]\n* [Pharmaceuticals Case Studies][183]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Pharmaceuticals | IPC][184]\n* [Maintaining CRT for Shipping Medicines & Pharmaceuticals | IPC][185]\n* [Food Case Studies][186]\n* [Expanding Reach for Mail-Order Beef with Insulated Shipping | IPC][187]\n* [Shipping Multiple Product Types Inside Single Container | IPC][188]\n* [How to Keep Ice Cream from Melting \u2013 Eco Insulated Pouch | IPC][189]\n* [Distributor Case Studies][190]\n* [Eliminating the Need for Refrigerated Trucking | IPC][191]\n* [White Papers][192]\n* [Pharmaceutical White Papers][193]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][194]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][195]\n* [2-8 \u00b0C Temperature Protection During Shipping | IPC][196]\n* [Shipment of Refrigerated Medical Vials Using PCM and PopupLiner Box Liner \u2013 Insulated\nProducts Corporation][197]\n* [Temperature-Controlled Packaging for Reusable Containers Using IPC\u2019s PopupLiner Thermal Box\nLiner \u2013 Insulated Products Corporation][198]\n* [Food White Papers][199]\n* [Insulation Solutions for Frozen Food Shipping | IPC][200]\n* [Enhanced Efficacy of Removable Thermal Box Liners | IPC][201]\n* [Overcoming the Problems of Shipping with EPS Coolers | IPC][202]\n* [Beverage White Papers][203]\n* [48-hour Thermal Protection for Shipping Wine | IPC][204]\n* [Shipping Frozen Human Milk Using Insulated Containers | IPC][205]\n* [Industrial White Papers][206]\n* [Freeze Protection when Shipping Water-based Paint & Grout | IPC][207]\n* [Insights][208]\n* [Jobs][209]\n* [Contact][210]\n* [Request Quote][211]\n* [Shipping Guides][212]\n\n[1]: #ajax-content-wrap\n[2]: https://ipcpack.com\n[3]: #sidewidgetarea\n[4]: https://ipcpack.com/products/\n[5]: https://"
