y, Cooling Horse Knee Wrap Full Coverage Leg Ice Boot Cold Pack 2 Wrap with 4 Gel Packs for Knee, Legs, Boots, and Hooves\n\nDesigned for equine care, this horse leg wrap combines thin gel packs with adjustable straps to cool legs comfortably after exercise. Packs slide into pockets for a secure fit and even contact. Durable materials and soft lining protect sensitive areas while speeding recovery.\n\nCheck Price\n\nBreast Ice Pack 2 Pack Gel Ice Pack for Breast Surgery, Reusable Nursing Ice Pack Hot or Cold Therapy Breast Pad for Breastfeeding, Engorgement Relief (Purple)\n\nThis two-pack of breast ice pads is sized for post-surgical comfort and breastfeeding relief, offering gentle, even cooling and reusable hot/cold therapy. Soft-backed pads fit discreetly in a bra or compression garment for convenient wear and recovery support.\n\nCheck Price\n\nShoulder Ice Pack Rotator Cuff Cold Therapy Reusable Cold Pack Shoulder Ice Wrap for Pain Relief, Recovery After Surgery, Swelling &#8211; Extra Large Size (Dark Blue)\n\nAn extra-large shoulder wrap offering broader coverage for significant swelling or post-op recovery. The reusable gel insert and wide attachment straps help distribute cooling evenly across the shoulder and upper arm. Built for comfort during extended wear.\n\nCheck Price\n\nSmall Ice Packs for Injuries, 14 Pack Round Ice Packs for Face, Hot and Cold Gel Ice Pack Circular Cold Compress with Cloth Backing &amp; Sleeve for Pain Relief, Toothaches, Breast Surgery\n\nA convenient set of small round gel packs for targeted relief of facial swelling, toothaches or localized post-surgery spots. Cloth-backed design sits comfortably on skin and fits into sleeves or dressings for flexible use. Handy for travel and first-aid kits.\n\nCheck Price\n\nCooling Gel Eye Mask 3D Soft Cold Eye Mask, Eye Ice Pack with Zero Eye Pressure Hot Cold Therapy Blackout Sleep Mask for Puffiness, Dark Circles, Dry Eyes, Headaches and Stress Relief\n\nThis 3D cooling gel eye mask is shaped to avoid pressure on the eyelids while providing blackout comfort for rest and therapy. Use chilled for puffiness and headaches or warmed for soothing dry-eye relief. Soft materials and balanced weight support relaxation.\n\nCheck Price\n\nOur Mission\n\nNEWGO\u2019s mission is to deliver reliable, evidence-informed hot and cold therapy that helps people recover faster, reduce pain, and regain comfort in daily life. We believe therapeutic products should be simple to use, thoughtfully designed, and built to last. By integrating clinical feedback into every development cycle, NEWGO ice pack solutions \u2014 including our shoulder cold wraps, knee and ankle options, and eye mask designs \u2014 are made to meet real recovery needs. We emphasize clear instructions, safe materials, and robust manufacturing processes so customers feel confident using cold and warm therapy at home, in clinics, or on the go. Sustainability is part of our vision: longer-lasting products, recyclable packaging, and sourcing practices that reduce environmental impact. We invest in education, supporting guides, and responsive support so each purchase becomes a trusted tool in long-term wellness. Our aim is to be recognized for consistent quality, transparent practices, and products that prioritize user safety and satisfaction \u2014 creating healthier routines for families, athletes, and medical recovery patients.\n\nVIEW CATALOG\n\nOur Motto\n\nSimple therapy, better recovery, everyday confidence.\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nQuality is our baseline. We design and test each gel pack and fabric wrap for puncture resistance, thermal retention, and long-term durability so you get dependable performance day after day. Try one risk-free and feel the difference.\n\nVariety that fits real life \u2014 from targeted eye masks and shoulder wraps to knee, ankle and nursing pads. Our range covers post-surgery recovery, sport care and everyday aches. Find the size and style that works for you.\n\nWe stand behind every product with helpful guides and friendly customer support. If you need usage tips or warranty help, our team responds quickly to ensure a smooth after-sale experience. Reach out anytime for support.\n\nFair pricing without cutting corners \u2014 we balance material quality, manufacturing standards and honest margins so you get lasting value. Practical therapy shouldn\u2019t be expensive; compare features and savings with confidence.\n\nModern design meets function: soft-touch fabrics, contoured gel pads, adjustable straps and leak-resistant seals. We iterate with clinicians and users to keep products intuitive, comfortable and contemporary. Explore the innovation.\n\nVIEW CATALOG\n\nReviews from our clients\n\nI use my NEWGO eye mask most evenings and when headaches hit during long workdays. The dual hot and cold function is genuinely useful \u2014 I alternate daily: chilled for puffiness after screen-heavy afternoons, warmed for dry-eye relief before bed. It\u2019s comfortable, sits without pinching, and the gel weight is reassuring rather than bulky. Over the past three months I\u2019ve used it about four times a week; it replaces messy washcloths and saves time. Fabric is soft and skin-friendly, and the size is generous without being cumbersome. Great value compared with single-use compresses; one minor note is it takes a couple more minutes in the microwave to reach the perfect warmth than the manual suggested, but I prefer the control.\n\nHannah Walker\n\nI bought this eye mask after reading positive reviews and I\u2019m happy to add mine. The construction is solid and the adjustable strap fits everyone in our house; the calming color feels relaxing. We store it in its sealed bag in the fridge so it\u2019s always ready for tired or itchy eyes \u2014 it\u2019s been a lifesaver during hayfever season. My teenage sons even use it after long gaming or study sessions to reduce redness and fatigue. It\u2019s also handy after screen-heavy workdays; five minutes of cool compression noticeably reduces puffiness. The only minor downside is sharing: we\u2019ll order an extra since one is hard to rotate during busy weeks. Overall a friendly, well-made eye mask that encourages short, restorative breaks.\n\nMelissa Grant\n\nAfter a forehead hematoma, my doctor suggested warm compresses; this heatable mask was a far better solution than a water bottle. I followed the recommended heating steps and added brief 5-second bursts to dial in comfort; the pad stayed warm for about 15 minutes with steady, gentle compression that didn\u2019t hurt. Compared with cold washcloths and loose ice packs, this product provided uniform contact and avoided leaks or awkward folding, which helped reduce swelling more predictably. I used it twice daily during the first week and appreciated how easy it was to reheat quickly. One limitation: if you need longer than 15\u201320 minutes of warmth, you\u2019ll need to reheat more often, but the convenience and consistent compression make it worth keeping in a recovery kit.\n\nDaniel Ortega\n\nI had a lumpectomy last week and these packs were indispensable. They were larger than I expected, which proved perfect \u2014 they cover the area well and lie flat if frozen correctly. One side is durable plastic and the other is a soft, velvety cloth that\u2019s kind to incision sites; I slipped a pack into my bra and held it with a compression band for the first 48 hours. My elbows used to get sore holding ice, so having something that tucks in and stays put was a huge relief. Packaging was simple and the packs felt well made. I\u2019d advise freezing them flat to avoid bumps and having them ready before surgery so you\u2019re not scrambling when you get home. Practical, comforting and highly recommended for post-op recovery.\n\nClaire Hernandez\n\nAfter five months of regular use, the wine cooler sleeve has outperformed similar sleeves I\u2019ve owned. The contoured design hugs bottles tightly so more of the surface touches the gel, which speeds chilling and evens out the temperature. I use it weekly \u2014 for patio dinners and last-minute guests \u2014 and even used it for champagne recently with no loss of performance. The sleeve hasn\u2019t shown wear or delamination and stays flexible after repeated freezing cycles. It\u2019"
          }
