harmaceuticals\n* Perishable foods and beverages\n* Health and beauty products\n* Floral arrangements and fresh-cut flowers\n* Agricultural and dairy products\n\n### What Should I Do to Order Samples of EcoGel\u2122?\n\nContact us \u2014 we\u2019ll be happy to discuss samples with you and [answer any questions.][138]\n\n### How Do Users Dispose of EcoGel\u2122 Gel Packs?\n\nAlthough EcoGel\u2122 packs are nontoxic and noncaustic, they are not drain-safe and may clog pipes.\nTherefore, we recommend disposing of the gel by emptying it into the trash and recycling the plastic\nfilm with your plastic bags.\n\nEcoGel\u2122 gel packs have the same disposal requirements as Glacier Ice\u2122 gel packs. This [VIDEO][139]\nexplains how to dispose of them.\n\n[PS-Logo-White with tagline][PS-Logo-White with tagline]\n\n## Solutions\n* [Life Sciences][140]\n* [Perishables][141]\n* [Specialty][142]\n* [Life Sciences][143]\n* [Perishables][144]\n* [Specialty][145]\n\n## Products\n* [Shipping Ice Packs][146]\n* [Eco-Friendly Ice Packs][147]\n* [Precision Ice Packs][148]\n* [Physical Therapy][149]\n* [Shipping Ice Packs][150]\n* [Eco-Friendly Ice Packs][151]\n* [Precision Ice Packs][152]\n* [Physical Therapy][153]\n\n## Resources\n* [Business FAQ][154]\n* [Consumer FAQ][155]\n* [Disposal Instructions][156]\n* [Blog][157]\n* [Business FAQ][158]\n* [Consumer FAQ][159]\n* [Disposal Instructions][160]\n* [Blog][161]\n\n## About\n* [About Us][162]\n* [Location][163]\n* [Success Stories][164]\n* [Join our Team][165]\n* [About Us][166]\n* [Location][167]\n* [Success Stories][168]\n* [Join our Team][169]\n\n## Pelton Shepherd Industries\n\n## 1-800-BLUE-ICE\n\n3120 W. March Lane\nStockton, CA 9"
