            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n\n### [1-800-COLD-HOT][2]\n\n[ Linkedin ][3]\n* [About][4]\n* [About Us][5]\n* [Quality & Compliance][6]\n* [Market Segments][7]\n* [Sustainability][8]\n* [Careers][9]\n* Products\n* [Refrigerants][10]\n* [Drain Friendly Gel Packs][11]\n* [Flexible PCM Mats][12]\n* [Interlocking Hard Bottle PCMs][13]\n* [Flexible Water Blankets][14]\n* [Durable Leak-Proof Gel Packs][15]\n* [Economy Gel Packs][16]\n* [Cost-Effective PCM Packs][17]\n* [Hard Bottle PCMs][18]\n* [Coolers & Insulation][19]\n* [Recyclable Coolers][20]\n* [Biodegradable Coolers][21]\n* [Rugged EPP Coolers][22]\n* [Durable EPS Coolers with ARCEL][23]\n* [PCM Mailers][24]\n* [Controlled Room Temperature Mailers][25]\n* [Refrigerated Mailers][26]\n* [Qualified Solutions][27]\n* Control Room Temperature\n* [CRT Recyclable Packaging][28]\n* [CRT Long Duration Cube][29]\n* [CRT Validated Packaging][30]\n* [CRT Rugged, Returnable Packaging][31]\n* [Refrigerated][32]\n* [Recyclable Packaging: Refrigerated][33]\n* [Long Duration Cube: Refrigerated][34]\n* [Validated Packaging: Refrigerated][35]\n* [Water & Gel-Based Packaging: Refrigerated][36]\n* [Rugged Packaging: Refrigerated][37]\n* Frozen\n* [Recyclable Packaging: Frozen][38]\n* [Long Duration Cubes: Frozen][39]\n* [Rugged Returnable Packaging: Frozen][40]\n* [Custom Solutions][41]\n* [Lab Services][42]\n* [Resources][43]\n* [Document Library][44]\n* [News & Education][45]\n* [Guide to Packaging Disposal][46]\n* [About Qualified Cold Chain Packaging][47]\n* [Professional & Regulatory Groups][48]\n* [Contact Us][49]\nMenu\n* [About][50]\n* [About Us][51]\n* [Quality & Compliance][52]\n* [Market Segments][53]\n* [Sustainability][54]\n* [Careers][55]\n* Products\n* [Refrigerants][56]\n* [Drain Friendly Gel Packs][57]\n* [Flexible PCM Mats][58]\n* [Interlocking Hard Bottle PCMs][59]\n* [Flexible Water Blankets][60]\n* [Durable Leak-Proof Gel Packs][61]\n* [Economy Gel Packs][62]\n* [Cost-Effective PCM Packs][63]\n* [Hard Bottle PCMs][64]\n* [Coolers & Insulation][65]\n* [Recyclable Coolers][66]\n* [Biodegradable Coolers][67]\n* [Rugged EPP Coolers][68]\n* [Durable EPS Coolers with ARCEL][69]\n* [PCM Mailers][70]\n* [Controlled Room Temperature Mailers][71]\n* [Refrigerated Mailers][72]\n* [Qualified Solutions][73]\n* Control Room Temperature\n* [CRT Recyclable Packaging][74]\n* [CRT Long Duration Cube][75]\n* [CRT Validated Packaging][76]\n* [CRT Rugged, Returnable Packaging][77]\n* [Refrigerated][78]\n* [Recyclable Packaging: Refrigerated][79]\n* [Long Duration Cube: Refrigerated][80]\n* [Validated Packaging: Refrigerated][81]\n* [Water & Gel-Based Packaging: Refrigerated][82]\n* [Rugged Packaging: Refrigerated][83]\n* Frozen\n* [Recyclable Packaging: Frozen][84]\n* [Long Duration Cubes: Frozen][85]\n* [Rugged Returnable Packaging: Frozen][86]\n* [Custom Solutions][87]\n* [Lab Services][88]\n* [Resources][89]\n* [Document Library][90]\n* [News & Education][91]\n* [Guide to Packaging Disposal][92]\n* [About Qualified Cold Chain Packaging][93]\n* [Professional & Regulatory Groups][94]\n* [Contact Us][95]\n\n# TempAid Lab Services\n\n###### Our state of the art lab is ready to assist our customers with their thermal testing and\n###### package validating needs. Successful cold chain handling of temperature sensitive products\n###### requires specialized services and expertise. Look to TempAid and our on-site testing facility\n###### to test and validate your products across the entire cold chain.\n\n#### Temperature and Environmental Package Testing\n\n[Thermal Packaging Design][96]\n\nCustomers count on us to develop advanced packaging systems that ensure reliable protection for\ntemperature-sensitive products through rigorous physical and thermal testing. Our custom designs are\nengineered to safeguard your products during transit, ensuring they meet all necessary product\nefficacy and patient safety standards. We offer a packaging system that delivers Innovation, product\nintegrity, and peace of mind.\n\n[Package Validation Testing][97]\n\nValidate your packaging systems through comprehensive testing, including temperature mapping,\nthermal performance, drop, and vibration tests, to ensure they maintain the desired temperature\nrange, protect product quality during transit and storage, and are optimized for maximum reliability\nand performance.\n\nThis process ensures packaging reliability, regulatory compliance, and product integrity, reducing\nthe risk of spoilage or loss within the cold chain. After we collect the foundational requirements,\ntesting may include:\n* **Process validation** ensures that equipment consistently performs as expected, producing\nhigh-quality parts reliably. This involves confirming that critical operations, like sealing and\nforming, are not only repeatable but dependable in every run.\n* **Transit testing **puts the packaging system to the test by simulating the stresses of\nsterilization, handling, and transportation. The goal is to ensure the package can endure these\nconditions while maintaining its sterile barrier and other essential properties.\n* **Accelerated Age Testing** evaluates the packaging\u2019s ability to maintain its critical functions\nover time, ensuring long-term reliability.\n\nWe conduct comprehensive validation testing, leveraging data from ISTA protocols, third-party\nstudies, and customer feedback to evaluate packaging performance in real-world conditions.\n\n[Walk-in Temperature Chamber Testing][98]\n\nWalk-in temperature chamber testing simulates various environmental conditions within an enclosed\nspace and is designed to control temperature and, often, humidity levels. Chamber testing offers\nrepeatable and consistent performance supported by data capture and enables compliance with 21 CFR\nPart 11.\n\nValidating packaging solutions under controlled ambient, refrigerated, and frozen temperature\nprofiles allows you to benefit from top-quality product performance and enjoy world-class service\nsolutions. This ensures packaging designs can withstand extreme conditions and maintain their\nintegrity, safeguarding the quality and safety of your products throughout their logistical journey.\n\nThis process ensures packaging reliability, regulatory compliance, and product integrity, reducing\nthe risk of spoilage or loss within the cold chain. After we collect the foundational requirements,\ntesting may include:\n* **Process validation** ensures that equipment consistently performs as expected, producing\nhigh-quality parts reliably. This involves confirming that critical operations, like sealing and\nforming, are not only repeatable but dependable in every run.\n* **Transit testing **puts the packaging system to the test by simulating the stresses of\nsterilization, handling, and transportation. The goal is to ensure the package can endure these\nconditions while maintaining its sterile barrier and other essential properties.\n* **Accelerated Age Testing** evaluates the packaging\u2019s ability to maintain its critical functions\nover time, ensuring long-term reliability.\n\nWe conduct comprehensive validation testing, leveraging data from ISTA protocols, third-party\nstudies, and customer feedback to evaluate packaging performance in real-world conditions.\n\n#### Mechanical and Physical Package Testing\n\n[R-Value Testing][99]\n\nReducing temperature fluctuations that could compromise the efficacy of sensitive products requires\nthat you ensure product integrity during transportation and storage. This can be done by carefully\nevaluating how well the packaging system resists heat transfer. R-Value testing involves exposing\nthe packaging to controlled temperature variations, tracking the temperature changes, and\ncalculating its thermal resistance (R-value).\n\nDoing this allows us to assess how effective coolers and insulated containers are at maintaining the\nnecessary temperature range. If issues are discovered, we can then select and configure the best\npackaging materials for your needs.\n\n[Specific Heat Measurement Testing][100]\n\nUtilizing the ASTM C1784 method, we analyze how much heat energy is required to raise a material\u2019s\ntemperature. This information is important for predicting the temperature stability of\npharmaceutical products under various environmental conditions.\n\nBy understanding the specific heat characteristics of their packaging, our clients can better\nanticipate temperature changes and mold strategies to mitigate risks related to thermal excursions,\nensuring that their products remain effective and safe for patient use.\n\n[ISTA Distribution Testing][101]\n\nAssess your packaging\u2019s performance under real-world shipping conditions. Although we currently\npartner with Orora\u2019s lab for these capabilities, we understand that shock, vibration, and\ncompression can significantly impact product integrity during transport. By simulating these\nconditions, we provide our clients with valuable data that informs their packaging decisions,\nensuring that their products withstand the rigors of the supply chain while maintaining quality and\nefficacy.\n\nBy understanding the specific heat characteristics of their packaging, our clients can better\nanticipate temperature changes and mold strategies to mitigate risks related to thermal excursions,\nensuring that their products remain effective and safe for patient use.\n\n[Primary Package Testing][102]\n\nTesting for seals and leaks is a proactive measure that ensures packaging integrity is uncompromised\nand protected against contamination and product loss. It safeguards patient safety and enhances\noverall trust in pharmaceutical products. Seal pull and leak testing adheres to ASTM-based Standard\nOperating Procedures (SOPs).\n\nBy understanding the specific heat characteristics of their packaging, our clients can better\nanticipate temperature changes and mold strategies to mitigate risks related to thermal excursions,\nensuring that their products remain effective and safe for patient use.\n\n[Accelerated Aging Testing ][103]\n\nSimulating long-term aging processes helps our clients understand how their products will perform\nover time. It allows for proactive adjustments in storage and handling practices, ensuring that\nefficacy and safety are preserved throughout their shelf life.\n\nBy understanding the specific heat characteristics of their packaging, our clients can better\nanticipate temperature changes and mold strategies to mitigate risks related to thermal excursions,\nensuring that their products remain effective and safe for patient use.\n\n#### Temperature Mapping and Validation Services\n\n[Shipping Lane Mapping][104]\n\nIdentify optimal routes, modes of transportation, and handling procedures to ensure products are\ntransported within the desired temperature range. Lane mapping has benefits, including improved\nvisibility into shipping logistics, identification of potential temperature excursions, proactive\nrisk mitigation, reduced product spoilage, enhanced product quality and safety, and regulatory\ncompliance. The TempAid team can help ensure the integrity and stability of your\ntemperature-sensitive products throughout the supply chain, minimizing the risk of product\ndegradation and loss.\n\n[Warehouse Mapping][105]\n\nWarehouse temperature mapping involves monitoring and analyzing temperature variations within a\nstorage facility to ensure proper conditions for temperature-sensitive products. The process\nconsists of mounting properly configured data loggers to monitor and analyze temperature variations\nwithin a storage facility to identify hot or cold spots that could compromise drug efficacy and\npatient safety.\n\nBy integrating with broader temperature mapping and validation services; warehouse mapping supports\nregulatory compliance, reduces spoilage risks, and informs better packaging design. Continuous\nenvironmental control enables companies to make immediate adjustments to safeguard product quality.\n\n[Freezer, Truck, and Equipment Mapping][106]\n\nTemperature mapping for freezers, trucks, and other refrigerated equipment is conducted in a more\ncontrolled, smaller space but requires precise monitoring due to the limited area and insulation\nproperties"
          },
