            "url": "https://gipatlantic.com/about/our-beliefs/",
            "text": "[ [GIP Atlantic] ][1]\n* [Capabilities][2]\n* [People][3]\n* [Projects][4]\n* [Employment][5]\n* [Indigenous Relations][6]\n* [Contact][7]\n[Construction workers in safety gear stand in front of a large opening in a concrete wall,\nsurrounded by heavy machinery, chains, and cut concrete sections at a construction site.]\n\n# Our Beliefs\n\nWe specialize in getting the job done.\n\n## Hard Work, Integrity, and Teamwork at the Heart of Our Success\n\nAt GIP Atlantic, we believe in rolling up our sleeves and getting the job done right. With decades\nof experience, our team thrives in challenging environments, tackling tough problems with passion,\ndetermination, and a can-do attitude.\n\nBuilt on a foundation of hard work and mutual respect, we are a trusted partner known for\nreliability and excellence. We work together, supporting one another and our clients every step of\nthe way.\n\nOur commitment to safety, environmental responsibility, and community well-being guides everything\nwe do. We continuously invest in improving our people and processes to deliver superior results\nwithout compromising our core values.\n\nWhen the call comes, we put on our boots and go to work\u2014because at GIP Atlantic, we don\u2019t quit until\nthe job is done.\n\n### About\n* [One Of Canada's Best Managed Companies][8]\n* [Hard work][9]\n* [Our Beliefs][10]\n* [Community][11]\n* [HSEQ][12]\n\n## Proof Is In the Projects\n\nOur capabilities are best demonstrated in the range and scale of work that we\u2019ve completed. Browse\nour projects to see our team at work on some of our country\u2019s largest projects.\n\n[View Projects][13]\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][14]\n\n\u00a92026 Green Infrastructure Partners. All rights reserved.\n* [Sitemap][15]\n* [Legal][16]\n* Feedback\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][17]\n* [Capabilities][18]\n* [People][19]\n* [Projects][20]\n* [Employment][21]\n* [Indigenous Relations][22]\n* [Contact][23]\n* [Sales & Rentals][24]\n* [About][25]\n* [Media Room][26]\n\nVisit our social media\n\nFill out the form below to leave feedback about the website and your browsing experience.\n\nEmail\nMessage\nSubmit\n\n## Search Green Infrastructure Partners\n\nSearch for:\n\nCancel\n\n[1]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[2]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[3]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[4]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[5]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[6]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[7]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[8]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/one-canadas-best-managed-companies/\n[9]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hard-work/\n[10]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/our-beliefs/\n[11]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/community/\n[12]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hseq/\n[13]: http://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[14]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[15]: https://gipatlantic.com/?page_id=12\n[16]: https://gipatlantic.com/legal/\n[17]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[18]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[19]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[20]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[21]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[22]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[23]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[24]: https://gipatlantic.com/sales-rentals/\n[25]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/\n[26]: https://gipatlantic.com/media-room/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://gipatlantic.com/about/hseq/",
            "text": "[ [GIP Atlantic] ][1]\n* [Capabilities][2]\n* [People][3]\n* [Projects][4]\n* [Employment][5]\n* [Indigenous Relations][6]\n* [Contact][7]\n[Two workers wearing safety vests, harnesses, and white hard hats are seen from behind, standing\noutdoors at an industrial site with blurred equipment in the background.]\n\n# HSEQ\n\nKeeping our people and communities safe is our top priority.\n\n## Health and Safety\n\nWe\u2019re relentlessly committed to protecting ourselves, our colleagues, and the environments in which\nwe work.\n\nAt GIP Atlantic, we\u2019ve built our business on active participation by everyone, every day, in every\njob to achieve safety excellence. We promote a zero incident policy for employees, subcontractors,\nproperty and the environment. Every employee, at every level, is responsible and accountable for our\nsafety initiatives.\n\nWe believe sound health and safety performance is fundamental to our successful business\nperformance, and we commit to minimizing the risks of injury or ill health to people and damage to\nproperty or business processes. Our safety performance requires establishing procedures and\nprograms, conducting training, contractor-employee involvement, routine self-evaluation and\ncontinuous improvement. We strive to incorporate recognized best practices into every program, seek\ninput from all of our resources for improvement, and evaluate the application and success of\nprograms on an ongoing basis.\n\n### Quality\n\nAt GIP Atlantic, we know we have to stay innovative, energetic, and adaptive. Backed by solid\nmanagement systems, everyday we work to improve product and performance. Our commitment to these\nsystems assure that our projects are safe, on schedule, on budget, and meet regulatory requirements.\n\nThrough employee training and education, we aspire to exceed client expectations, and industry\nstandards and look to strengthen our workforce today and tomorrow. We believe our strong team of\ninternal quality control personnel are industry leaders and with every hand on every tool focused on\nattaining the highest standards, our clients and partners can be sure we are delivering the best\nproduct, performance and value in the industry.\n\nWe have several divisions registered to the ISO 9001:2015 Quality Management System standard, and\nthis System outlines the organizational structure, responsibilities, processes and resources to\nensure effectiveness and continuous improvement.\n\n### Environment\n\nJob performance isn\u2019t just about quality service and meeting client expectations, it\u2019s also about\nprotecting the environments and communities in which we work. At GIP Atlantic, always improving our\nenvironmental performance is a fundamental part of building our business. On each project we work to\nmeet and exceed environmental regulations/requirements and these environmental considerations are\nweaved throughout initial project planning, operations and decommissioning. We promote sustainable\ndevelopment through pollution prevention, waste minimization and recycling, wherever possible, and\nwe\u2019ve developed systems and teams to support our commitment to the environment.\n\nOur environmental management team provides direction and guidance on every project to ensure that\nour work is planned, designed, and constructed to be consistent with our Environmental Policy and\nour goal of environmental excellence.\n\n### Safety Awards\n* * Natural Resources Magazine 2018 Industry Excellence Award for Health and Safety. [Read more][8].\n* Award of Excellence for Environmental Leadership & Innovation from the Heavy Civil Association\nof Newfoundland and Labrador (HCANL)\n* Award of Excellence for Safety from the Heavy Civil Association of Newfoundland and Labrador\n(HCANL)\n* Winner of 10 Silver Coin Awards from ExxonMobil for our dedication to safety on the Hebron\nProject\n\n### Certifications\n\n## Proof Is In the Projects\n\nOur capabilities are best demonstrated in the range and scale of work that we\u2019ve completed. Browse\nour projects to see our team at work on some of our country\u2019s largest projects.\n\n[View Projects][9]\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][10]\n\n\u00a92026 Green Infrastructure Partners. All rights reserved.\n* [Sitemap][11]\n* [Legal][12]\n* Feedback\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][13]\n* [Capabilities][14]\n* [People][15]\n* [Projects][16]\n* [Employment][17]\n* [Indigenous Relations][18]\n* [Contact][19]\n* [Sales & Rentals][20]\n* [About][21]\n* [Media Room][22]\n\nVisit our social media\n\nFill out the form below to leave feedback about the website and your browsing experience.\n\nEmail\nMessage\nSubmit\n\n## Search Green Infrastructure Partners\n\nSearch for:\n\nCancel\n\n[1]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[2]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[3]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[4]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[5]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[6]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[7]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[8]: https://www.naturalresourcesmagazine.net/?article=industry-excellence-awards-3&page=3.\n[9]: http://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[10]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[11]: https://gipatlantic.com/?page_id=12\n[12]: https://gipatlantic.com/legal/\n[13]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[14]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[15]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[16]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[17]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[18]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[19]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[20]: https://gipatlantic.com/sales-rentals/\n[21]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/\n[22]: https://gipatlantic.com/media-room/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://gipatlantic.com/about/one-canadas-best-managed-companies/",
            "text": "[ [GIP Atlantic] ][1]\n* [Capabilities][2]\n* [People][3]\n* [Projects][4]\n* [Employment][5]\n* [Indigenous Relations][6]\n* [Contact][7]\n[A smiling woman in safety gear, including a helmet and harness, stands at the top of a wind turbine\nwith a scenic green landscape and blue sky in the background.]\n\n# One Of Canada\u2019s Best Managed Companies\n\nCelebrating excellence in Canadian business leadership.\n\n## GIP Atlantic Achieves Platinum Club Status with Canada\u2019s Best Managed Companies Program\n\nNow in its 25th year, Canada\u2019s Best Managed Companies is one of the country\u2019s leading business\nawards programs recognizing Canadian-owned and managed companies for innovative, world-class\nbusiness practices. Every year, hundreds of entrepreneurial companies compete for this designation\nin a rigorous and independent process that evaluates the calibre of their management abilities and\npractices.\n\nGIP Atlantic recently achieved Platinum Club status with the Canada\u2019s Best Managed Companies program\nby retaining its Best Managed designation for seven consecutive years or more.\n\n[Canada Best Managed Companies - Platinum member]\n\n### About\n* [One Of Canada's Best Managed Companies][8]\n* [Hard work][9]\n* [Our Beliefs][10]\n* [Community][11]\n* [HSEQ][12]\n\n## Proof Is In the Projects\n\nOur capabilities are best demonstrated in the range and scale of work that we\u2019ve completed. Browse\nour projects to see our team at work on some of our country\u2019s largest projects.\n\n[View Projects][13]\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][14]\n\n\u00a92026 Green Infrastructure Partners. All rights reserved.\n* [Sitemap][15]\n* [Legal][16]\n* Feedback\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][17]\n* [Capabilities][18]\n* [People][19]\n* [Projects][20]\n* [Employment][21]\n* [Indigenous Relations][22]\n* [Contact][23]\n* [Sales & Rentals][24]\n* [About][25]\n* [Media Room][26]\n\nVisit our social media\n\nFill out the form below to leave feedback about the website and your browsing experience.\n\nEmail\nMessage\nSubmit\n\n## Search Green Infrastructure Partners\n\nSearch for:\n\nCancel\n\n[1]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[2]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[3]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[4]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[5]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[6]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[7]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[8]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/one-canadas-best-managed-companies/\n[9]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hard-work/\n[10]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/our-beliefs/\n[11]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/community/\n[12]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hseq/\n[13]: http://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[14]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[15]: https://gipatlantic.com/?page_id=12\n[16]: https://gipatlantic.com/legal/\n[17]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[18]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[19]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[20]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[21]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[22]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[23]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[24]: https://gipatlantic.com/sales-rentals/\n[25]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/\n[26]: https://gipatlantic.com/media-room/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://gipatlantic.com/about/hard-work/",
            "text": "[ [GIP Atlantic] ][1]\n* [Capabilities][2]\n* [People][3]\n* [Projects][4]\n* [Employment][5]\n* [Indigenous Relations][6]\n* [Contact][7]\n[A construction worker wearing a white hard hat, safety glasses, and a reflective vest stands next\nto stacked metal mesh panels at an outdoor worksite.]\n\n# Hard work\n\nis our tradition at GIP Atlantic.\n\n[Play Video][8]\n\n## Diverse Expertise United by a Strong Work Ethic\n\nGIP Atlantic\u2019s strength lies in its diverse and skilled team, including engineers, welders,\nelectricians, accountants, heavy equipment operators, carpenters, and many more professionals from\nvarious backgrounds. While our expertise and roles vary, we share a common thread: a strong work\nethic, unwavering character, and a passionate spirit.\n\nThis dedication and unity set GIP Atlantic apart from competitors, driving us to deliver exceptional\nresults on every project. Our culture of hard work and commitment is deeply rooted in our tradition\n\u2014 a story we proudly share in our corporate video, *Hard Work is Our Tradition*.\n\nDiscover how our people and values make GIP Atlantic a trusted leader in the industry.\n\n### About\n* [One Of Canada's Best Managed Companies][9]\n* [Hard work][10]\n* [Our Beliefs][11]\n* [Community][12]\n* [HSEQ][13]\n\n## Proof Is In the Projects\n\nOur capabilities are best demonstrated in the range and scale of work that we\u2019ve completed. Browse\nour projects to see our team at work on some of our country\u2019s largest projects.\n\n[View Projects][14]\n\n## Media\n\nClick on the thumbnail to play the video.\n\n[ [Youtube Video] ][15]\n\n**Warning**: Attempt to read property \"post_excerpt\" on null in\n**/nas/content/live/gipatlanticprd/wp-content/themes/jac/lib/get.php** on line **776**\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][16]\n\n\u00a92026 Green Infrastructure Partners. All rights reserved.\n* [Sitemap][17]\n* [Legal][18]\n* Feedback\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][19]\n* [Capabilities][20]\n* [People][21]\n* [Projects][22]\n* [Employment][23]\n* [Indigenous Relations][24]\n* [Contact][25]\n* [Sales & Rentals][26]\n* [About][27]\n* [Media Room][28]\n\nVisit our social media\n\nFill out the form below to leave feedback about the website and your browsing experience.\n\nEmail\nMessage\nSubmit\n\n## Search Green Infrastructure Partners\n\nSearch for:\n\nCancel\n\n[1]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[2]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[3]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[4]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[5]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[6]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[7]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[8]: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XpIeqac3-E\n[9]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/one-canadas-best-managed-companies/\n[10]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hard-work/\n[11]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/our-beliefs/\n[12]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/community/\n[13]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/hseq/\n[14]: http://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[15]: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9XpIeqac3-E\n[16]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[17]: https://gipatlantic.com/?page_id=12\n[18]: https://gipatlantic.com/legal/\n[19]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[20]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[21]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[22]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[23]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[24]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[25]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[26]: https://gipatlantic.com/sales-rentals/\n[27]: https://gipatlantic.com/about/\n[28]: https://gipatlantic.com/media-room/"
          },
          {
            "url": "https://gipatlantic.com/about/community/",
            "text": "[ [GIP Atlantic] ][1]\n* [Capabilities][2]\n* [People][3]\n* [Projects][4]\n* [Employment][5]\n* [Indigenous Relations][6]\n* [Contact][7]\n[Three children sitting and smiling, with one holding a stuffed animal, in front of a large\nceremonial check for $10,000 made out to \"Children]\n\n# Community\n\nWe care about our people, our communities, and our province, which is why GIP Atlantic has a long\nhistory of partnering with and investing in the places we work and live. We support\nvarious charities and not-for- profit organizations through donations and sponsorships, and take\ngreat pride in championing our employees who volunteer for charitable or community projects. We are\nproud to operate with a benevolent spirit and consider our community involvement a fundamental part\nof who we are. Community investment focus areas are: Mental Health, Education, Community Need, Arts,\nDiversity, Safety, and Environment. If you would like to learn more about GIP Atlantic\u2019s Community\nInvestment please contact [[email protected]][8].\n\n[$250,000 to Canadian Mental Health Association of NL]\n\n### $250,000 to Canadian Mental Health Association of NL\n\nToday GIP Atlantic launched a partnership with the Canadian Mental Health Association of\nNewfoundland and Labrador, and committed $250,000 to the organization over a 5-year period.\nExecutive Chairman Larry Puddister, and Kelsey Puddister of the Jacob Puddister Memorial Foundation\nare pictured here presenting a $250,000 cheque to CMHANL Executive Director Dan Goodyear.\n\n[Donation to the Janeway]\n\n### Donation to the Janeway\n\nGIP Atlantic donated $100,000 to the Janeway Children\u2019s Hospital Foundation which is is a registered\ncharitable organization created to raise funds to meet the financial needs of the Janeway Children\u2019s\nHealth and Rehabilitation Centre. Funds raised go to capital projects, equipment, research, and\nprograms directly related to the health and welfare of Newfoundland and Labrador Children.\n\n[Legacy Gifts for Education and Mental Health]\n\n### Legacy Gifts for Education and Mental Health\n\nGIP Atlantic has two significant planned giving initiatives. One is a $2 million legacy gift to fund\na research chair at Memorial University; the second is a $2 million legacy gift for the Healthcare\nFoundation to fund NL mental health and addictions programming.\n\n[Supporting WRDC\u2019s Techsploration]\n\n### Supporting WRDC\u2019s Techsploration\n\nGIP Atlantic is a long-time supporter of WRDC\u2019s Techsploration program which aims to provide young\nwomen with opportunities to explore trades, technical and technology-related occupations, while\ncreating an awareness about the critical role of work in their lives.\n\n## Proof Is In the Projects\n\nOur capabilities are best demonstrated in the range and scale of work that we\u2019ve completed. Browse\nour projects to see our team at work on some of our country\u2019s largest projects.\n\n[View Projects][9]\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][10]\n\n\u00a92026 Green Infrastructure Partners. All rights reserved.\n* [Sitemap][11]\n* [Legal][12]\n* Feedback\n\n[ [GIP Atlantic] ][13]\n* [Capabilities][14]\n* [People][15]\n* [Projects][16]\n* [Employment][17]\n* [Indigenous Relations][18]\n* [Contact][19]\n* [Sales & Rentals][20]\n* [About][21]\n* [Media Room][22]\n\nVisit our social media\n\nFill out the form below to leave feedback about the website and your browsing experience.\n\nEmail\nMessage\nSubmit\n\n## Search Green Infrastructure Partners\n\nSearch for:\n\nCancel\n\n[1]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[2]: https://gipatlantic.com/capabilities/\n[3]: https://gipatlantic.com/people/\n[4]: https://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[5]: https://gipatlantic.com/employment/\n[6]: https://gipatlantic.com/indigenous-relations/\n[7]: https://gipatlantic.com/contact/\n[8]: /cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#2a59474b4645444f536a4d435a4304494547\n[9]: http://gipatlantic.com/projects/\n[10]: https://gipatlantic.com/\n[11]: h