            "url": "https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/box-liners/renewliner-recycling/",
            "text": "[Skip to content][1]\n* [Giveback][2]\n* [Do Better][3]\n* [(r) Value][4]\n* [Resources][5]\n* [Thermal Ecolab][6]\n* [Cold Chain Exchange][7]\n* [The Thermalist][8]\n* [Thermasure][9]\n* [Careers][10]\n* [Contact Us][11]\n[ [TSS Logo] ][12]\nMENUMENU\n* [Industries][13]\n* * * [Telehealth Pharmacy][14]\n* [Specialty Pharmacy][15]\n* * [Mail Order Pharmacy][16]\n* [Animal Health][17]\n* * [Independent Pharmacy][18]\n* [Food and Beverage][19]\n* * [Retail & Home Delivery Pharmacy][20]\n* [Botanicals][21]\n* [Products][22]\n* * * [**Pre-Validated Shipping Kits**][23]\n* * **Mailers & Envelopes**\n* [Kangaroo Mailer][24]\n* [RenewMailer][25]\n* [DuraShield Envelopes][26]\n* * **Box Liners**\n* [Renewliner][27]\n* [DuraShield Box Liners][28]\n* * **Refrigerants**\n* [Gel Ice Packs][29]\n* * [Latest Innovation][30]\n* [Company][31]\n* * * [About TSS][32]\n* [History][33]\n* [TSS Innovation Advantage][34]\n* [TSS Locations][35]\n* [Sustainable Leadership][36]\n* [Industries][37]\n* [Telehealth Pharmacy][38]\n* [Specialty Pharmacy][39]\n* [Mail Order Pharmacy][40]\n* [Animal Health][41]\n* [Independent Pharmacy][42]\n* [Food and Beverage][43]\n* [Retail & Home Delivery Pharmacy][44]\n* [Botanicals][45]\n* [Products][46]\n* [TSS Pre-Validated Solutions][47]\n* [Mailer & Envelopes][48]\n* [Kangaroo Mailer][49]\n* [RenewMailer][50]\n* [DuraShield Envelopes][51]\n* [Box Liners][52]\n* [Renewliner][53]\n* [DuraShield Box Liners][54]\n* [Refrigerants][55]\n* [Gel Ice Packs][56]\n* [Latest Innovation][57]\n* [Company][58]\n* [About TSS][59]\n* [History][60]\n* [TSS Innovation Advantage][61]\n* [Sustainable Leadership][62]\n* [Giveback][63]\n* [Do Better][64]\n* [(r) Value][65]\n* [Resources][66]\n* [Thermal Ecolab][67]\n* [Cold Chain Exchange Strategies][68]\n* [Thermasure][69]\n* [Careers][70]\n* [Contact Us][71]\nRenewliner Recycling[Thomas Evans][72]2024-07-29T15:29:25-04:00\n\n# Renewliner:\n# The world\u2019s first curbside recyclable insulated box liners.\n\nSourced from the globe\u2019s most recyclable plastic, PET, Renewliner debuts the world\u2019s first curbside\nrecyclable insulated box liner shipping system.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos.\n\nRenewliner is made from polyethylene terephthalate (PET), a strong, lightweight plastic that is used\nin everything from water bottles to carpeting and one of the only materials in existence with the\ntechnology to be infinitely recyclable.\n\nPET is the most recycled plastic in the U.S and worldwide, with more than 1.5 billion pounds of used\nPET being recovered in the United States each year for recycling. A 2010 study found that producing\none ton of recycled PET, compared to one ton of virgin PET, saves 48 million BTUs of energy and\nreduces greenhouse gas emissions by 3,000 pounds.\n\nPET is not only recyclable, it also has an incredibly low carbon footprint compared to alternative\npackaging materials like cotton, denim, and paper. PET enables TSS to reduce the environmental\nimpact twofold, by tackling the current pollution issues (removing material from the waste streams\nand giving them a second life), while also creating a product will be recycled again and again.\n\n### Is Renewliner curbside recyclable?\n\nYes, Renewliner and PET are curbside recyclable. Here\u2019s how.\n\n### Step 1: Curbside Collection\n\nYou can put Renewliner directly into your recycling containers for curbside collection. Nearly every\nmunicipal recycling program in North America and Europe accepts PET bottles and containers, which\ncan be easily identified by #1 stamped into the bottom or side of the container.\n\nAlways check with your local recycling office to see what is accepted in your area.\n\n### Step 2: Separation\n\nRecyclable materials are separated at the recycling facility, with glass and metal being transferred\ninto their own recycling streams and high-value plastics like PET being separated from other\nplastics, which would reduce the quality of PET and limit its ability to be reused.\n\n### Step 3: Transportation\n\nAfter PET is collected and separated, it is compressed for transportation to processing facilities.\nUnlike other recyclable materials, PET is extremely lightweight and can be compressed into small\nbales that reduce emissions during transportation.\n\n### Step 4: Processing\n\nCompressed bales of PET are processed by thorough washing and re-melting or by chemically breaking\nit down to its component materials to make a new PET resin.\n\n### How NOT to recycle Renewliner.\n\n1. Don\u2019t tear off the outer layer.\n2. Don\u2019t put it in your garbage can.\n3. Don\u2019t put it in your home compost.\n\n### Renewliner is at the forefront of sustainability.\n\nThe only thermal packaging solution awarded Most Sustainable Temperature-Sensitive Project by Cold\nChain Global Forum.\n\nThe Cold Chain Global Forum is one of the most prestigious and credentialed organizations in the\nindustry, and Renewliner is the only thermal packaging solution to be recognized by the Cold Chain\nGlobal Forum as the \u201cMost Sustainable Temperature-Sensitive Project.\u201d Renewliner was awarded this\ndistinguished recognition because it is the world\u2019s first curbside recyclable insulated shipping\nsystem and uses closed-loop recycled material to create the most sustainable product on the market.\n\n100% Curbside\nRecyclable\n\nClosed Loop\nRecycled Material\n\nRemoves Waste\nFrom Refuse Stream\n\nReduced Carbon\nFootprint\n\nUSA Made\n\n### How is Renewliner and PET recycled?\n\nRather than being sent to a landfill, Renewliner and PET can be converted from post-consumer use\ninto a pellet that can be extruded into a usable form for PET products through a process called\nmechanical recycling.\n\nMechanical recycling does not allow material to be infinitely recycled, only chemical recycling does\nthis through a process that breaks the plastic down into it\u2019s building block chemical components to\nyield a virgin quality materials by removing contaminants, etc. Through an enzymatic process they\ncan raise or lower the intrinsic viscosity which is the main component that is reduced after each\nlife/recycle in a mechanical process.\n\nMechanical recycling is the most widely used process in the U.S. and globally. According to the\nreport \u201cMechanical Plastics Recycling \u2014 The Global Market\u201d by AMI, mechanical recycling surpassed 54\nmillion tons globally in 2022 and is projected to be nearly 55 million tons by 2030. Because\nmechanical recycling is widely available, it is a great solution to recycle Renewliner again and\nagain.\n\nTo certify that Renewliner is recyclable, it was subjected to a thorough testing process by\n[Palmetto Synthetics, LLC][73].\n\nEquipment Used\n\nFor the melt temperature, Palmetto Synthetics used a Fisher/Johns Melting Point Apparatus. For the\ncolor value, they used a DataColor 800.\n\n### Step 1:\n\nThe product is shredded into small pieces, which is then transported to a condensing unit to further\ndecreases the size of the pieces.\n\n### Step 2:\n\nA polymer is then introduced into the extrusion line to be vacuumed in a 2-zone vacuum system,\nremoving any volatiles or gasses.\n\n### Step 3:\n\nThe material is then filtered & injected through a dye where it gets cut into smaller pieces,\ncaptured in a water stream, and transferred through a quench loop.\n\n### Step 4:\n\nFinally, the material is sent to a dryer where water and pellets are separated. The pellets go into\nthe box, while the water is returned to the tank to be re-used \u2013 creating a closed-loop recycling\nprocess.\n\nResults\n\nAfter concluding its rigorous testing procedure, Palmetto Synthetics determined that PET is an\nexcellent candidate for recycling and Renewliner can be recycled for reuse.\n\n1. Given the various types of PET material that may be available for recycling, it is important to\nnote the following:\n1. The incoming raw material must be one hundred percent PET\u2014no blends of other\ntypes of polymers, such as nylon (PA), polypropylene (PP), or polyethylene (PE).\n2. The incoming raw material must be of similar intrinsic viscosity\u2014this includes\nlow-melt PET products that may be blended into the incoming raw material.\n\n2. Any deviation from the above can cause failures and downtime in the recycling process.\n\nHere is a video demonstration of the Renewliner/PET recycling process produced by Palmetto\nSynthetics.\n\nSorry, your browser doesn't support embedded videos.\n\n## What happens if my local collection group does not want to accept Renewliner?\n\nPET is fully recyclable, though some material recovery facilities (MRFs) in U.S. cities, counties\nand municipalities may not accept it. MRFs play a key role in the recycling ecosystem. A MRF is a\nfacility that sorts and processes mixed recyclable materials into new products through a combination\nof machinery, equipment, and human effort to sort and prepare the materials.\n\nThe U.S. recycling system has several major shortcomings that result in only 32.1% of waste being\neither recycled or composted. Some of these shortcomings occur in MRFs, which make their own\ndecisions about which products to accept.\n\nOne reason that MRFs may not accept Renewliner is because they are not equipped with the human and\nmachine resources to properly collect, remove and sort some recyclables from the waste stream.\nAnother reason is that they may not realize that Renewliner is 100% PET because it is a new product\nthat they have not seen before.\n\nTSS cannot control these independent businesses, nor their collection policies. Please check with\nyour local MRF for specific details in your area.\n\n6 Hamilton Lndg.\nSuites 160 + 175\nNovato, CA, 94949, US\n\n[415-389-5004][74]\n\n[sales@thermalshipping.com][75]\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2026\nThermal Shipping Solutions.\nAll rights reserved.\n\n[ista logo]\n\nIndustries\n\n[Telehealth Pharmacy][76]\n\n[Specialty Pharmacy][77]\n\n[Mail Order Pharmacy][78]\n\n[Animal Health][79]\n\n[Independent Pharmacy ][80]\n\n[Food & Beverage][81]\n\n[Retail & Home Delivery Pharmacy][82]\n\n[Botanicals][83]\n\nProducts\n\n[Pre-Validated Shipping Kits][84]\n\nMailer & Envelopes\n\n[Kangaroo Mailer][85]\n\n[RenewMailer][86]\n\n[DuraShield Envelopes][87]\n\nBox Liners\n\n[Renewliner][88]\n\n[DuraShield Box Liners][89]\n\nRefrigerants\n\n[Gel Ice Packs][90]\n\n[Latest Innovation][91]\n\nCompany\n\n[Who we are][92]\n\n[History][93]\n\n[TSS Advantage & Innovation][94]\n\n[Locations][95]\n\n[Sustainable Leadership][96]\n\nGiveback\n\n[Do Better][97]\n\n[(r) Value][98]\n\nResources\n\n[Thermal Ecolab][99]\n\n[Cold Chain Exchange][100]\n\n[Thermasure][101]\n\n[Careers][102]\n\n[Contact Us][103]\n\n[Privacy Policy][104]\n\n[Terms and Conditions][105]\n\n[Page load link][106]\n[ Go to Top ][107]\n\n[1]: #content\n[2]: #\n[3]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/giveback/our-impact-dodeca/\n[4]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/giveback/r-value/\n[5]: #\n[6]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/resources/thermal-ecolab/\n[7]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/resources/cold-chain-exchange/\n[8]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/resources/the-thermalist/\n[9]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/thermasure/\n[10]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/careers/\n[11]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/contact-us/\n[12]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/\n[13]: #\n[14]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/digital-telehealth-pharmacy/\n[15]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/specialty-pharmacy/\n[16]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/mail-order-pharmacy/\n[17]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/industries/animal-health/\n[18]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/independent-pharmacy/\n[19]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/food-and-beverage/\n[20]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/large-retail-pharmacy/\n[21]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/industries/botanicals/\n[22]: https://thermalshipping.com/products/\n[23]: https://thermalshipping.com/products/box-liners/tss-pre-validated-solutions/\n[24]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/mailer-envelopes/kangaroo-mailer/\n[25]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/mailer-envelopes/renewmailer/\n[26]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/mailer-envelopes/durashield-envelopes/\n[27]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/box-liners/renewliner/\n[28]: https://www.thermalshipping.com/products/box-liners/durashield-box-liners/\n[29]: https://www.thermalshipping.co"
