l Trials][196]\n* [ECONOMY][197]\nECONOMY\n* [U.S. Economy][198]\n* [Advance Monthly Sales][199]\n* [Consumer Price Index CPI][200]\n* [Producer Price Index PPI][201]\n* [Retail Inventories][202]\n* [Personal Income][203]\n* [Gross Domestic Product GDP][204]\n* [Money Supply][205]\n* [Industrial Production][206]\n* [Productivity][207]\n* [Employment Situation][208]\n* [U.S. International Trade][209]\n* [Factory Orders][210]\n* [Durable Goods][211]\n* [Construction Spending][212]\n* [Housing Starts][213]\n* [Vehicle Unit Sales][214]\n* [SCREENING][215]\nSCREENING\n* [Stock Screener][216]\n* [Stock Performance Screening][217]\n* [Profitability Screening][218]\n* [Valuation Screening][219]\n* [Dividend Screening][220]\n* [Financial Strength Screening][221]\n* [Efficiency Screening][222]\n* [Largest Companies][223]\n* [Management Effectiveness Screening][224]\n* [GLOSSARY][225]\nGLOSSARY\n* [Financial Terms][226]\n* [Technical Analysis][227]\n* Fundamental Analysis\n* Growth Rates\n* [Growth Rate Comparisons][228]\n* [Revenue][229]\n* [Gross Income][230]\n* [EBIT][231]\n* [Operating Income][232]\n* [Income Before Taxes][233]\n* [Income Taxes][234]\n* [Income from Cont. Operations][235]\n* [Net Income][236]\n* [EPS from Cont. Operations][237]\n* [EPS Net][238]\n* [Free Cash Flow][239]\n* [Net Cash Flow][240]\n* [Capital Expenditures][241]\n* Profitability\n* [Profitability Comparisons][242]\n* [Gross Profit Margin][243]\n* [Operating Profit Margin][244]\n* [EBITDA Margin][245]\n* [Net Profit Margin][246]\n* [Pre-Tax Profit Margin][247]\n* [Effective Tax Rate][248]\n* [Free Cash Flow Margin][249]\n* [Net Cash Flow Margin][250]\n* Valuation\n* [Valuation Comparisons][251]\n* [P/E Ratio TTM][252]\n* [P/S Ratio TTM][253]\n* [P/CF Ratio TTM][254]\n* [P/FCF Ratio TTM][255]\n* [Price to Book MRQ][256]\n* [Price to Tangible Book][257]\n* Management Effectiveness\n* [Management Effectiveness Comparisons][258]\n* [ROA Quarterly][259]\n* [ROI Quarterly][260]\n* [ROE Quarterly][261]\n* Financial Strength\n* [Financial Strength Comparisons][262]\n* [Quick Ratio][263]\n* [Working Capital][264]\n* [LT Debt to Equity][265]\n* [Debt to Equity][266]\n* [Leverage Ratio][267]\n* [Tangible Leverage][268]\n* [Interest Coverage][269]\n* [Debt Coverage][270]\n* [Working Cap. Per Revenue][271]\n* Efficiency\n* [Efficiency][272]\n* [Revenue per Employee][273]\n* [Income per Employee][274]\n* [Inventory Turnover][275]\n* [Asset Turnover][276]\n* [Receivables Turnover][277]\n* Dividend\n* [Dividend Comparisons][278]\n* [Dividend Growth][279]\n* [Dividend Payout][280]\n* [Energy Terms][281]\n* [Manufacturing Terms][282]\n* [Transportation Terms][283]\n* [Health Care][284]\n* [Insurance Terms][285]\n* [Economy Terms][286]\n* [Hotel & Leisure Terms][287]\n* [HELP][288]\nHELP\n* [Help][289]\n* [About Us][290]\n* [What is New][291]\n* [Terms of Use][292]\n* Licensing and Subscriptions\n* [Financial Data Downloads][293]\n* [API & Data Feed Access][294]\n* [OEM & Enterprise Licensing][295]\n* [Subscription Plans][296]\n* [AI Licensing][297]\n* [Terms of Use][298]\n* [Editorial Standards][299]\nIndustry Benchmarking\n\n# Know Exactly Where\n# a Company Stands\n# in Its Industry\n\nInstantly compare any company's margins, growth, valuation, and financial strength against every\npeer in its industry - backed by 20+ years of normalized data.\n\n[ Learn More About Benchmarking Data \u2192 ][300] [ Contact Data Team \u2192 ][301]\nNet Margin - Software Industry\nMSFT\n36.9%\nAAPL\n25.3%\nORCL\n21.7%\nSAP\n16.4%\n\u2605 YOU\n14.1%\nCRM\n10.2%\nSource: Financial filings \u00b7 TTM \u00b7 Updated daily\n110\nIndustries Covered\nCSV Files per Industry\n660+\nTotal Dataset Files\n20+ Yrs\nHistorical Depth\nDaily\nData Updates\n\nWhat Is Industry Benchmarking?\n\n## From Raw Financials to Competitive Context\n\nA company's net margin of 18% tells you very little on its own. Is that strong or weak? It depends\nentirely on the industry. CSIMarket's Industry Benchmarking layer wraps every financial metric in\n**peer-relative context** - so you always know whether a number is above average, below average, or\nan outlier.\n\nPre-built benchmarking reports covering profitability, growth, valuation, financial strength, and\nESG-related metrics across hundreds of industries - structured for risk, compliance, and financial\ncrime teams, including **AML and KYC workflows** such as source of wealth validation, as well as\nquantitative analysts who require peer-validated, audit-ready comparisons without building from raw\ndata.\n\nDesigned for **compliance, due diligence, onboarding, financed emissions reporting, and investment\nanalysis**, the dataset enables consistent validation of financial and sustainability profiles\nagainst industry benchmarks.\n\nAvailable as an **institutional-grade financial dataset** for financial institutions, delivered via\n**bulk data feeds, API access, or custom-scoped datasets** through our *Numbers on Your Desk*\nservice - via secure download or email.\n\n[ \u2193 Download Benchmarking Methodology & Coverage PDF ][302]\n\nAPI & Spreadsheet Integration\n\n### Connect Benchmarking Data Directly Into Your Workflow\n\nIndustry benchmarking datasets can be connected directly into Excel, Google Sheets, Power BI,\nTableau, Python, Snowflake, Databricks, internal dashboards, and AI-driven research systems using\nREST API access and bulk dataset delivery.\n\nBy connecting the API directly to Excel or Google Sheets, benchmarking and financial datasets can\nrefresh automatically whenever the spreadsheet is opened or updated \u2014 eliminating manual exports,\ncopy-pasting, and outdated static reports.\n\nThis allows analysts, investors, compliance teams, and researchers to work with continuously updated\nindustry benchmarks, profitability metrics, valuation data, growth analytics, and peer comparisons\ndirectly inside their existing spreadsheet models and dashboards.\n\n#### Excel & Google Sheets\n* Automated benchmarking dashboards\n* Live industry comparison worksheets\n* Dynamic valuation and profitability tracking\n* Custom screening and peer analysis models\n\n#### Enterprise & Analytics Platforms\n* Power BI and Tableau integration\n* Python and quantitative research workflows\n* Snowflake and Databricks connectivity\n* AI agents and automated research systems\n\nAPI access supports automated retrieval of updated benchmarking data, enabling scalable research,\nmonitoring, compliance, and quan"
