rm Architecture\n\n## Unified, AI integrated system of intelligence\n\nOne system to identify, investigate, monitor, and manage supplier risk with the speed and visibility\nteams need\n\nData Fabric\nIntelligence Engine\nWorkspace\n\nData Fabric\n\n## Unified source of supplier truth\n\nAggregated, normalized, and enriched supplier data in one centralized, trusted foundation\n* 250k+ supplier attributes and real-time news from 20+ data pipelines\n* Agentic intelligence to fetch, refresh, normalize, and resolve records across sources\n* Network graph mapping supplier hierarchies, dependencies, and relationships\n\nDecision intelligence\n\n## Data in. High-fidelity intelligence out.\n\nTurn supplier data into decision-quality risk signals and performance insight\n* AI-native risk detection, scoring, and alerts across supplier portfolios\n* Configurable frameworks to assess risk across 6+ domains\n* Intelligence integrated into the tools, workflows, and reports where teams work most\n\nIntelligent workspace\n\n## Where supplier decisions happen\n\nMonitor, analyze, and act in one AI-integrated workspace with alerts, tasks, and collaboration tools\n* Generate comprehensive AI supplier risk assessments in seconds\n* Continuously monitor suppliers with workflows to alert category owners, investigate issues, and\n  drive follow-up actions\n* Organize suppliers by category, region, or spend and collaborate on notes, approvals, and\n  remediation\n\n## Trusted by leading global enterprises\n\nCraft powers procurement intelligence for the world\u2019s most forward-thinking organizations.\n\n> \u201cI was able to build my portfolio in less than an hour, and with previous tools it would have\n> taken a week. I was overwhelmed by the intuitive nature, the capability, and the freedom.\u201d\n\nGlobal Category Manager, US Air Force\n\n\n[US Air Force Logo]\n[US Air Force Logo]\n\nResults\n\n90%\n\nreduction in time to deliver due diligence\n\n87%\n\nfaster supplier onboarding\n\nSolutions\n\n[View government solutions][26] [Get the gov eBook][27]\n\n> \u201cNo supplier is going to call you beforehand to tell you something negative is going to happen, so\n> using Craft to minimize risk much earlier has proved invaluable for us.\u201d\n\nDirector, Supply Chain & Sustainability\n\n\nResults\n\n2,000+\n\ncritical suppliers monitored\n\n95%\n\nof total procurement spend monitored\n\nSolutions\n\n[Read case study][28] [Explore the platform][29]\n\n> \u201cCraft has transformed our approach to supplier risk management with its intuitive platform,\n> delivering speed to value across our supplier engagements.\u201d\n\nProcurement Director\n\n\nResults\n\n100%\n\nof critical suppliers and partners monitored for financial, reputational, compliance, and cyber\nrisks\n\n> \u201cWe were investigating a geopolitical issue with a vendor. We used Craft to find 9 additional\n> n-tier network risks that we wouldn\u2019t have seen otherwise.\u201d\n\nDirector, Third-Party Risk Management\n\n\nResults\n\n968\n\nsuppliers continuously monitored\n\n40\n\nmonthly supplier risk assessment and qualification\n\nSolutions\n\n[View finserve solutions][30] [Download solution brief][31]\n\nBuilt for sectors that rely on resilience\n\n\n## Solutions for every industry\n\nFrom government agencies to research institutions, every sector faces growing pressure to move\nfaster and manage supplier risk with confidence. Craft delivers the intelligence each industry needs\nto stay compliant, resilient, and ready for what\u2019s next.\n\n[\n\nGovernment\n\nStrengthen supplier due diligence, visibility, and risk mitigation across federal programs.\n\nExplore government solutions\n\nExplore government solutions\n\n][32] [\n[Aerospace Icon]\n\nAerospace and Defense\n\nStreamline complex supplier risk management and safeguard mission-critical operations.\n\nExplore aerospace and defense solutions\n\nExplore aerospace and defense solutions\n\n][33] [\n\nHigher Education\n\nProtect research funding and ensure compliance across your institution and research ecosystem.\n\nExplore higher education solutions\n\nExplore higher education solutions\n\n][34] [\n\nFinancial Services\n\nManage third-party risk and regulatory compliance with trusted supplier intelligence.\n\nExplore financial services solutions\n\nExplore financial services solutions\n\n][35] [\n\nManufacturing\n\nIncrease visibility, reduce disruption, and build a more resilient supply network.\n\nExplore manufacturing solutions\n\nExplore manufacturing solutions\n\n][36]\n\n## Explore insights and perspectives from Craft\n* [\n  \n  Blog\n  \n  How Supply Chain Illumination Prep"
